('D-169','market-selection','Do not promote Session Pulse until a named prep-loss incident beats the exact free stack.','Doodle, Discord, Warhorn, Foundry, and ad-hoc messages are mandatory controls; category payment is insufficient without repeated product-specific preference.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-SESSION-PULSE-110',NULL),
('D-170','market-selection','Treat recurring GM-prep reports as recruiting evidence, not proof of a new product.','The pain is strong, but current premium and free prep suites occupy the broad workspace category.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-SCORECARD-111',NULL),
('D-171','market-product-boundary','Do not open a generic prep canvas, generic AI prep tool, or generic scheduling product from the fresh scan.','The defensible future wedge would be safe reuse of discarded preparation after a player pivot, and that requires a named failure and rights-safe fixture.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-SCORECARD-111',NULL),
