('D-234','market-selection','Open Zero-Prep Session Capsule only as a low-priority conditional challenger.','The minimum-configuration pain is recurring, but Dungeon Flow, Morelord Encounters, Encounter Forge, Mass Import, importer packages, premium adventures, and existing session-prep candidates occupy major portions of the job.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-ZERO-PREP-CAPSULE-131',NULL),
('D-235','market-product-boundary','Define Zero-Prep Session Capsule as user-owned orchestration, not AI content generation or a bundled adventure.','The differentiator must be a previewed, player-safe, reversible, time-boxed launch plan with cleanup and unsupported receipts; copied rules, publisher text, protected art, and competitor data are out of scope.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-ZERO-PREP-CAPSULE-131',NULL),
('D-236','market-selection','Require exact-alternative preference, non-zero WTP, pilots, runtime, rights, and second-VTT evidence before promotion.','The concept may only be a convenience bundle, and portability cannot be inferred from a shared manifest.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-ZERO-PREP-CAPSULE-131',NULL),
('D-237','market-selection','Demote the broad Zero-Prep Session Capsule after the SessionFlow incumbent correction.','SessionFlow now occupies the one-canvas session workspace and recaps, while Dungeon Flow and paid adventures cover import/content paths. Only a narrow disposable safety wrapper remains conditional and it has no product-specific WTP.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-ZERO-PREP-CORRECTION-132',NULL),
('D-238','market-selection','Open No-Spoiler Player Return Brief as a conditional challenger, not a selected product.','Monthly and irregular campaigns show absent-player and lore-recall pain, but Archivist Sync, Foundry Familiar, Campaign Codex, SessionFlow, LegendKeeper, and shared fog cover adjacent workflows.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-RETURN-BRIEF-133',NULL),
('D-239','market-product-boundary','Define Return Brief as GM-approved per-player spoiler-scoped re-entry, not a wiki, transcript, search box, or chatbot.','The differentiator is permissioned re-entry with redaction, contradiction, revocation, acknowledgement, and a safe next action.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-RETURN-BRIEF-133',NULL),
('D-240','market-selection','Require direct price choice, exact-alternative preference, two pilots, spoiler-safe runtime, rights, and second-VTT manifest evidence before promotion.','Category interest and assistant payment cannot be transferred to a new Return Brief; a shared neutral ledger cannot prove runtime parity.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-RETURN-BRIEF-133',NULL),
('D-241','market-selection','Demote No-Spoiler Player Return Brief after the direct payment and incumbent correction.','Archivist, LegendKeeper, and Tavern Scribe now provide paid campaign-memory and missed-session workflows that cover the broad claim.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-RETURN-CORRECTION-134',NULL),
('D-242','market-product-boundary','Retain Return Brief audience, spoiler, contradiction, acknowledgement, and revocation records only as reusable assets.','The records may support a future Foundry-local failure, but they are not evidence of a standalone product while direct incumbents cover the buyer job.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-RETURN-CORRECTION-134',NULL),
('D-243','market-selection','Move Game Night Preflight / World Doctor to the first empirical buyer gate without selecting it.','Update and recovery pain has high consequence and a plausible payer segment, but exact Foundry, recovery, hosting, and duplicate-world alternatives create a high proof burden.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-WORLD-DOCTOR-PAYER-135',NULL),
('D-244','market-product-boundary','Require World Doctor price, exact-alternative preference, two disposable-copy pilots, runtime safety, rights/privacy, and second-VTT receipt evidence before promotion.','A read-only evidence-linked rehearsal may be differentiated, but static compatibility metadata and category maintenance payment cannot prove actual buyer conversion or safe execution.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-WORLD-DOCTOR-PAYER-135',NULL),
('D-245','market-selection','Demote World Doctor after the direct incumbent and payer correction.','Foundry core, paid hosting, version choice, backups, save points, and duplicate-world practice close the broad safety claim; behavioral rehearsal remains unproven.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-WORLD-DOCTOR-CORRECTION-136',NULL),
('D-246','market-product-boundary','Retain World Doctor only as a clone-based behavioral smoke suite and neutral diagnostic receipt.','A compatibility dashboard, backup browser, or live repair tool would duplicate current capabilities or create unacceptable false-green and mutation risk.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-WORLD-DOCTOR-CORRECTION-136',NULL),
('D-247','market-selection','Treat prepared content and professional session value as the strongest current payment anchors.','The marketplace makes content and booked-table outcomes visibly valuable, while broad utility modules and player-economy workflows are crowded.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-MARKET-SCAN-137',NULL),
('D-248','market-selection','Open Attendance-Resilient Side Session only as a bounded paid/professional payer test.','Variable attendance can waste booked revenue and preparation, but home tables often have free social workarounds and current premium adventures already cover generic drop-in content.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-MARKET-SCAN-137',NULL),
('D-249','market-selection','Continue the wide ordinary-table search in parallel; do not select a product after Pass 137.','No fresh broad utility passed direct competition and product-specific WTP. The attendance test is a narrow economic control, not permission to settle on a professional-only niche.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-MARKET-SCAN-137',NULL),
('D-250','market-selection','Reject generic Combat Replay, Combat Analytics, Battle Recorder, and Undo Assistant as new products.','Battle Replay, Combat Stats, Damage Log, PF2e Combater, and native/system workflows now cover the broad surface; current interest does not establish product-specific WTP.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-COMBAT-REPLAY-138',NULL),
('D-251','market-product-boundary','Retain combat event envelopes, visibility filters, timelines, correction receipts, and export as reusable assets only.','A future player-safe debrief would require a distinct repeated learning failure, price choice, pilot, system semantics, and hidden-state safety.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-COMBAT-REPLAY-138',NULL),
('D-252','market-selection','Demote generic Player Compass, player cockpit, character creator, source manager, and mobile panel claims after the current-package correction.','Player Pilot, Foundry Navigator, system HUDs, hidden-tab/tutorial workflows, and current D&D5e character builders already cover the broad pain; only a named residual failure is testable.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-PLAYER-CORRECTION-139',NULL),
('D-253','market-product-boundary','Retain player focus, accessibility, capability explanation, visibility, source policy, and progress contracts as reusable assets.','These contracts may support a future wedge but do not establish a standalone product or WTP.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-PLAYER-CORRECTION-139',NULL),
('D-254','market-selection','Treat generic drop-in content as occupied but retain Attendance-Resilient Side Session as a bounded content-plus-workflow test.','Drop-in Dungeons, Prepared! 2, Dragonshorn, Omnipresence, Oronder, SessionFlow, and premium cinematic adventures cover the broad claims; no-canon variable-party safe exit is the only residual boundary.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-ADAPTIVE-COMPETITION-140',NULL),
('D-255','market-selection','Run Attendance-Resilient Side Session as the first empirical gate without selecting it.','Paid/professional and high-variance organizers have measurable booking/prep loss, but home groups have free alternatives and product-specific WTP is unproven.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-ADAPTIVE-COMPETITION-140',NULL),
('D-256','market-selection','Continue the ordinary-table search if Attendance-Resilient Side Session proves professional-only.','A niche professional product may be viable but does not satisfy the broad ordinary-table objective by itself.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-ADAPTIVE-COMPETITION-140',NULL);

INSERT OR REPLACE INTO kb_open_items(item_id,item_class,title,problem,next_action,evidence_needed,priority,status,owner,source_id) VALUES
('O-086','research','Run World Doctor buyer-price and alternative-choice test','Update anxiety is strong, but qualified GMs may prefer delaying updates, backups, or free/current modules.','Recruit long-running or paid Foundry GMs with a recent incident; compare current workaround with a 30-second World Doctor demo at $15/$25/$39/no purchase.','7/10 recent incident or near miss, 5/10 preference, 3 non-zero choices, 2 disposable-copy pilots, and explicit alternative rejection.','P0','open','product-research','SRC-WORLD-DOCTOR-74'),
('O-087','implementation','Build a read-only World Doctor disposable-copy rehearsal fixture','A preflight claim is unsafe unless it proves no live-world mutation and can distinguish package metadata from actual behavior.','Clone a disposable world, record package/assets/dependencies, run a controlled update or compatibility change, execute smoke checks, and emit a recovery receipt.','No live writes, deterministic report, evidence paths, authoritative reread, reversible restore, and captured unsupported cases.','P0','open','runtime','SRC-WORLD-DOCTOR-73'),
('O-088','research','Compare World Doctor against current Foundry recovery and audit tools','Core backups, Sephral, Asset Auditor, Find the Culprit, FileSmith, Scene Packer, and manual support may solve the buyer''s real job.','Show each alternative against the same recent incident and record time-to-decision, confidence, selected price, and pilot commitment.','Buyer chooses preflight rehearsal for a specific failure and pays or schedules the pilot.','P1','open','product-research','SRC-WORLD-DOCTOR-73'),
('O-089','implementation','Prove a second-VTT read-only diagnostic packet','Foundry-first diagnostics may not generalize to hosted or extension-based VTTs.','After Foundry proof, implement a read-only Roll20 or Owlbear probe with package/asset/check receipt semantics.','One second VTT reports health without claiming migration or repair parity and preserves licensing/permission boundaries.','P2','open','runtime','SRC-WORLD-DOCTOR-74'),
('O-090','research','Run Tactical Sketchbook buyer-choice and price test','A direct drawing request includes real-money language, but core drawings, free modules, external whiteboards, and a premium early-access direction may be good enough.','Recruit drawing-heavy live-play GMs; run the 30-second route/label/scope demo against native drawings, Precise/Dungeon Draw/Quickdraw, Gambit, and the buyer''s manual workaround at $10/$20/$30/no purchase.','7/10 recent drawing failure, 5/10 preference, 3 non-zero choices, 2 three-session pilots, and explicit alternative rejection.','P0','open','product-research','SRC-SKETCHBOOK-77'),
('O-091','implementation','Build a Tactical Sketchbook Foundry permission and snapshot fixture','Temporary and private annotations can leak to players, survive longer than intended, or mutate the source scene unexpectedly.','Use a disposable two-client Foundry v14 scene with GM-only, party, temporary, saved, undo, reconnect, and export cases.','No scope leak, deterministic cleanup, snapshot/reload convergence, explicit source mutation confirmation, and reversible layer promotion.','P0','open','runtime','SRC-SKETCHBOOK-77'),
('O-092','implementation','Define a neutral vtt-sketch annotation record','Foundry, Roll20, and Owlbear differ in drawing objects, permissions, storage, and mobile behavior.','Define strokes/shapes/text, scope, anchor, style, author, revision, expiry, and export target without claiming identical rendering.','Foundry record round-trips; unsupported fields are explicit; no copied art or hosted storage is required.','P1','open','runtime','SRC-SKETCHBOOK-77'),
('O-093','research','Compare Tactical Sketchbook against the premium drawing direction and free alternatives','A premium competitor may remove the gap before the product is built, while a free module may already solve the exact failure.','Test the same live-play fixture with core, Precise, Dungeon Draw, Quickdraw, Gambit if available, and an external whiteboard.','Time-to-first-mark, cleanup, permission safety, source mutation, buyer preference, price choice, and pilot commitment.','P1','open','product-research','SRC-SKETCHBOOK-76'),
('O-094','research','Run Adventure Navigator buyer-choice and price test','A fifteen-minute search incident is concrete, but maintained free search modules, Campaign Codex, World & Campaign Builder, and external PDF/book search may be good enough.','Recruit adventure-running GMs; compare current tools with a 30-second active-scene context demo at $15/$25/$39/no purchase.','7/10 recent lookup failure, 5/10 preference, 3 non-zero choices, 2 three-session pilots, and explicit alternative rejection.','P0','open','product-research','SRC-ADVENTURE-NAV-81'),
('O-095','implementation','Build an Adventure Navigator local content-index fixture','Indexing can leak GM-only text, copy publisher content, mis-rank source pages, or become stale after edits.','Use a synthetic adventure-shaped world with journals, headings, scenes, notes, actors, items, cross-links, player clues, and GM secrets; test active-scene context and reconnect/reindex.','Exact source links, no permission leak, local-only index, deterministic reindex, stale-link visibility, and no copied publisher text.','P0','open','runtime','SRC-ADVENTURE-NAV-81'),
('O-096','research','Compare Adventure Navigator against current search, journal, and campaign tools','The market may already be satisfied by Search and Highlight, Simple SearchBar, Quick Insert, Monk''s Enhanced Journal, Campaign Codex, or World & Campaign Builder.','Run the same incident with each maintained substitute and record time-to-source, false positives, link accuracy, preference, price, and pilot commitment.','Contextual runbook wins a repeated incident, not only a benchmark search; buyer chooses a non-zero price.','P1','open','product-research','SRC-ADVENTURE-NAV-80'),
('O-097','implementation','Define a neutral context-index record and one second-VTT boundary','Roll20 handouts and Owlbear extensions differ from Foundry journals, scene notes, permissions, and storage.','Define source ID/page, anchor, relationship edges, excerpt hash, scope, rank explanation, and pin/dismiss state; then test one read-only second-VTT adapter after Foundry proof.','Foundry round-trip, explicit unsupported fields, source links rather than copied content, and no parity claim without second proof.','P2','open','runtime','SRC-ADVENTURE-NAV-81'),
('O-098','research','Test whether the time-saved demo beats AI copilots without cloud dependency','Some GMs may prefer Simulacrum or another AI copilot, while others reject AI or external indexing for privacy and trust.','Show local deterministic context and AI-copilot alternatives separately; record trust, privacy, latency, false-positive, and price objections.','Buyer chooses the local product for a concrete incident and accepts the no-cloud boundary.','P1','open','product-research','SRC-ADVENTURE-NAV-80'),
('O-099','implementation','Prove Adventure Navigator permission and stale-index correctness','A local index may surface GM-only content, stale source links, or copied publisher text after edits and migrations.','Build a disposable synthetic world with multiple journal pages, map notes, user permissions, linked actors/items/scenes, an edit, a delete, and a reconnect; run deterministic reindex and source-open checks.','No hidden content in player result set, exact source-link receipts, explicit stale status, deterministic rebuild, and no new copied adventure text.','P0','open','runtime','SRC-ADVENTURE-NAV-82'),
('O-100','implementation','Prove one read-only second-VTT context-index boundary after Foundry proof','Roll20 and Owlbear expose different handout, extension, storage, and permission surfaces.','After the Foundry fixture, implement one adapter that reports source links and context without claiming equivalent search or document semantics.','One second VTT passes permitted-source filtering and explicit unsupported fields; no parity or rights claim is made from the neutral record alone.','P2','open','runtime','SRC-ADVENTURE-NAV-82'),
('O-101','research','Run the cross-candidate Adventure Navigator buyer pilot','The newest candidate has a concrete incident but may lose to existing search, campaign, PDF, or AI workflows.','Recruit adventure-running GMs; compare current workflow and named alternatives with a 30-second contextual runbook at $15/$25/$39/no purchase.','7/10 lookup problem, 5/10 preference, 3 non-zero price choices, 2 three-session pilots, and explicit alternative rejection.','P0','open','product-research','SRC-MARKET-SCORECARD-83'),
('O-102','research','Run a separate World Doctor buyer and disposable-copy arm','Update safety may attract higher-value GMs but has narrower demand and greater risk of false reassurance.','Recruit long-running/module-heavy GMs; compare backups/auditors and test $15/$25/$39/no purchase without mutating a live world.','7/10 incident or near miss, 5/10 preference, 3 non-zero price choices, 2 disposable-copy pilots, and deterministic safety receipt.','P1','open','product-research','SRC-MARKET-SCORECARD-83'),
('O-103','research','Run Rapid Encounter Board buyer-choice and price test','The community reports scene-creation friction, but active MapForge/FA Nexus/Moulinette/import workflows may already satisfy improvisation-heavy GMs.','Recruit GMs who create an unplanned encounter at least monthly; time their current workflow and compare the temporary staging demo at $15/$25/$39/no purchase.','7/10 recent staging failure, 5/10 preference, 3 non-zero choices, 2 three-session pilots, and explicit alternative rejection.','P1','open','product-research','SRC-RAPID-SCENE-85'),
('O-104','implementation','Build a disposable Rapid Encounter Board Foundry fixture','Temporary layers may leak, promotion may mutate the wrong scene, user-owned assets may be duplicated, and reconnect may leave stale board state.','Use a synthetic scene with background, grid, tokens, temporary wall/light/label layers, GM/party/private scopes, promotion, discard, reconnect, and player view.','No scope leak, deterministic cleanup, explicit native promotion, stable asset references, reconnect convergence, and no bundled publisher content.','P1','open','runtime','SRC-RAPID-SCENE-85'),
('O-105','implementation','Define a neutral encounter-board package and one second-VTT boundary','Foundry scenes, Roll20 pages/objects, and Owlbear scenes/extensions have different storage and permission semantics.','Define background reference, grid, token refs, wall/light segments, labels, scope, expiry, and promotion state; test one read-only adapter after Foundry proof.','Foundry round-trip, explicit unsupported fields, source references not copied assets, and no parity claim from the neutral shape alone.','P2','open','runtime','SRC-RAPID-SCENE-85'),
('O-106','research','Compare Rapid Encounter Board against current map-authoring workflows','MapForge, FA Nexus, Moulinette, Mass Import, Scene Express, external map makers, and the buyer''s manual process may win on assets or flexibility.','Run one improvised encounter with each available alternative and record time-to-ready, cleanup, scope safety, asset friction, preference, price, and pilot commitment.','Staging lane wins repeated live incidents rather than only a demo; buyer rejects at least one existing alternative and chooses a non-zero price.','P2','open','product-research','SRC-RAPID-SCENE-85'),
('O-107','research','Run a mandatory Rapid Encounter Board versus MapForge head-to-head','MapForge already has a strong commercial demo and category payment signal, so native Foundry-only controls are an insufficient comparison.','Recruit MapForge-accessible improvisation-heavy GMs and time the same encounter-staging task with MapForge and Rapid Encounter Board.','Rapid Encounter Board wins time-to-ready or scope/promotion safety for a repeated incident and the buyer rejects MapForge for that reason.','P1','open','product-research','SRC-RAPID-SCENE-86'),
('O-108','research','Test Rapid Encounter Board one-time versus subscription/no-purchase positioning','MapForge''s Patreon access creates a price and support anchor, but subscription fatigue may be a preference rather than a product gap.','After the head-to-head task, randomize one-time $15/$25/$39, subscription-like support, and no-purchase offers; record the reason and pilot commitment.','Three non-zero choices, two three-session pilots, and explicit evidence that the offerâ€”not only the categoryâ€”is preferred.','P1','open','product-research','SRC-RAPID-SCENE-86'),
('O-109','research','Recheck Rapid Encounter Board portability after the buyer comparison','A portable encounter package may be valuable, but adding export before Foundry buyer proof could dilute the live-staging product.','Only after a Foundry preference, test the neutral package in one Roll20 or Owlbear read-only adapter and record unsupported fields.','Buyer still values portability, source references are rights-safe, and no equivalent-runtime claim is made from the package shape alone.','P2','open','product-research','SRC-RAPID-SCENE-86'),
('O-110','research','Run TableStart buyer-choice and price test','Player complexity is mixed and existing free/premium controls may be good enough.','Recruit table owners with a recent onboarding or return-to-play incident; compare core/current setup, Hide UI, Player Pilot, and TableStart at $10/$20/$30/no purchase.','7/10 recent failures, 5/10 preference, 3 non-zero choices, 2 three-session pilots, and explicit rejection of named alternatives.','P1','open','product-research','SRC-PLAYER-START-87'),
('O-111','implementation','Build a disposable TableStart session-recipe fixture','Per-player scope, actor/scene changes, fallback, and reconnect may leave players stuck or expose actions to the wrong user.','Test new, returning, and one-shot players with synthetic actors/scenes, role-specific actions, ready/AFK state, fallback, reconnect, and permission changes.','No cross-player leak, deterministic fallback, actor/scene convergence, reconnect recovery, and no live-world mutation outside intended state.','P1','open','runtime','SRC-PLAYER-START-88'),
('O-112','research','Compare TableStart against the full player-experience substitute set','A buyer may only need Hide UI, Player Pilot, a tutorial, Claim Your Hero, Character Builder, AFK Ready Check, or SessionFlow.','Run the same onboarding and return-to-play tasks with each available alternative and record help requests, wrong actions, time, preference, price, and pilot commitment.','TableStart wins a repeated incident that the chosen alternative cannot solve and the buyer chooses a non-zero price.','P1','open','product-research','SRC-PLAYER-START-88'),
('O-113','implementation','Define a neutral TableStart session-recipe package','Foundry actor/sheet/scene APIs differ from Roll20 and Owlbear player surfaces and storage.','Define recipe, role, beat, action descriptors, references, completion, and fallback; document unsupported fields before any export claim.','Foundry round-trip with permission safety and explicit unsupported fields; no bundled publisher/rulebook content.','P2','open','runtime','SRC-PLAYER-START-88'),
('O-114','implementation','Probe one second VTT only after TableStart buyer proof','A portable recipe shape does not prove equivalent guided actions or permissions.','After Foundry buyer/runtime proof, build a read-only Roll20 or Owlbear adapter that renders a recipe and records completion without mutation.','One second-VTT adapter preserves role scope, references, completion, and fallback or clearly reports unsupported behavior.','P2','open','runtime','SRC-PLAYER-START-88'),
('O-115','research','Test the TableStart marketing message against the incumbent category','â€œMake Foundry easy for playersâ€ is too broad and directly occupied.','A/B test the one-minute first-action/return-to-play promise against a mobile-sheet, clean-UI, and character-creation message with qualified table owners.','The session-recipe message wins attention and non-zero price choice for a concrete repeated incident.','P2','open','product-research','SRC-PLAYER-START-88'),
('O-116','research','Run Tabletop Bridge buyer-choice and price test','In-person pain is visible, but current modules may already be good enough and the payer pool may be narrow.','Recruit recurring in-person/hybrid GMs; compare their current stack, named modules, and Tabletop Bridge at $20/$35/$50/no purchase.','7/10 recent coordination failures, 5/10 preference, 3 non-zero choices, 2 three-session pilots, and explicit alternative rejection.','P1','open','product-research','SRC-TABLETOP-89'),
('O-117','implementation','Build a cold-start Tabletop Bridge setup/recovery fixture','A shared display may show secrets, a player device may stale, physical-roll entry may duplicate or drop a roll, and a scene policy may overload clients.','Use synthetic GM, TV, two player devices, physical/digital roll modes, secret handout, preload policy, disconnect/reconnect, and in-person/remote profile switching.','No secret leak, no duplicate/drop, deterministic client recovery, measured load policy, and no live-world mutation outside intended state.','P1','open','runtime','SRC-TABLETOP-90'),
('O-118','research','Compare Tabletop Bridge against the full current module/device stack','The buyer may only need Monk''s Common Display, Physical Play Dice, TouchVTT, Player Pilot, Gaming Table, Ninjo''s In-Person Tools, Lock View, or a second browser.','Run the same cold-start and mid-session recovery task with each available alternative and record setup steps, failures, preference, price, and pilot commitment.','Tabletop Bridge wins a repeated setup/recovery incident rather than only presenting a nicer dashboard.','P1','open','product-research','SRC-TABLETOP-90'),
('O-119','implementation','Define a neutral table-session record','Foundry display, player, device, and dice APIs differ from Roll20 and Owlbear extensions.','Define display/input roles, device capabilities, secret scope, scene policy, client status, profile state, and explicit unsupported fields.','Foundry round-trip, permission safety, and no hardware/provider dependency; unsupported fields documented.','P2','open','runtime','SRC-TABLETOP-90'),
('O-120','implementation','Probe one second VTT only after Tabletop Bridge buyer/runtime proof','Equivalent display routing and physical-dice orchestration may not be expressible on another VTT.','After Foundry proof, implement a read-only Roll20 or Owlbear profile renderer and record unsupported controls.','One second-VTT adapter preserves role/profile metadata or clearly reports unsupported behavior without parity claims.','P2','open','runtime','SRC-TABLETOP-90'),
('O-121','research','Test whether orchestration beats a feature bundle in marketing','A â€œone-click in-person modeâ€ message may be less compelling than physical dice, mobile control, or TV display individually.','A/B test the setup-and-recovery promise against component-feature messages with qualified hybrid GMs.','Orchestration wins attention, non-zero price choice, and pilot commitment for a named repeated incident.','P2','open','product-research','SRC-TABLETOP-90'),
('O-122','research','Find product-specific payment evidence before reviving Tabletop Bridge','Current package competition closes the feature gap and free components may be sufficient.','Search for a paid orchestration/reliability alternative or a qualified buyer who already pays for this exact setup/recovery job.','A paid alternative, named unresolved failure, or three independent non-zero price choices before re-opening the buyer arm.','P2','open','product-research','SRC-TABLETOP-91'),
('O-123','research','Keep Tabletop Bridge out of implementation while parked','Building another integrated table mode would duplicate current packages and create a high-support, weak-portability surface.','Do not build until O-122 passes; preserve only the neutral table-session boundary as a reusable asset.','Explicit paid wedge, runtime failure fixture, and one second-VTT feasibility boundary.','P2','open','product-research','SRC-TABLETOP-91'),
('O-124','research','Run VTT BridgeCheck buyer-choice and price test','Migration pain and importer payment evidence are real, but the exact importer may be sufficient and migration is episodic.','Recruit active migrating GMs; compare exact importer plus manual cleanup with BridgeCheck at $10/$25/$50/$75/no purchase.','7/10 named post-import failures, 5/10 preference, 3 non-zero choices, 2 real campaign pilots, and explicit alternative rejection.','P0','open','product-research','SRC-BRIDGECHECK-92'),
('O-125','implementation','Build a disposable BridgeCheck import/rehearsal fixture','A validator that mutates the live world, misses permission leaks, or gives false green results is unsafe.','Use synthetic Roll20-like, DDB-like, and Foundry versioned exports with actors, scenes, walls, lights, tiles, journals, links, permissions, missing files, duplicates, and unsupported fields.','No live mutation, accurate diff, deterministic rerun, permission/secret safety, explicit unsupported fields, and auditable receipt.','P0','open','runtime','SRC-BRIDGECHECK-93'),
('O-126','research','Compare BridgeCheck against the exact source importer and cleanup path','A generic receipt may add little value after DDB-Importer, VTTA, R20Converter, PDF-to-Foundry, or Phils Map Migrator.','Run one migration through each available source path and record unresolved work, confidence, time, price, and pilot commitment.','BridgeCheck wins a named repeated or deadline-critical failure and the buyer pays for assurance rather than importing alone.','P1','open','product-research','SRC-BRIDGECHECK-93'),
('O-127','implementation','Define the neutral transfer-receipt contract','A shared contract may overpromise parity across source and target VTT APIs.','Define source/target IDs, document kinds, asset fingerprints, link edges, schema versions, permissions, checks, repair proposals, review decisions, and unsupported fields.','Foundry round-trip plus explicit source/target limitations; no copied publisher content.','P1','open','runtime','SRC-BRIDGECHECK-93'),
('O-128','implementation','Prove permission and licensing boundaries for user-owned exports','Migration inspection can expose secrets, scrape content, or store copyrighted text if its data model is too broad.','Use references/fingerprints/check results, permission fixtures, revocation, and no-content-copy policies before any real adapter.','No unauthorized discovery, no bypassed access controls, no redistributed publisher data, and auditable deletion of temporary extracts.','P1','open','runtime','SRC-BRIDGECHECK-93'),
('O-129','implementation','Probe one second-VTT receipt adapter after Foundry buyer/runtime proof','Roll20, D&D Beyond, Fantasy Grounds, and Owlbear do not share equivalent export, storage, or permissions.','Implement one read-only second-VTT receipt renderer after Foundry passes and document unsupported fields.','One second-VTT adapter preserves receipt semantics without claiming converter parity or source-rights equivalence.','P2','open','runtime','SRC-BRIDGECHECK-93'),
('O-130','research','Keep LootFlow rejected unless a qualified table names a repeated transaction failure','The broad workflow is current-package crowded and the premium demo is already occupied.','Do not recruit or implement until a GM and player report a repeated failure with the current stack and choose a price test.','A named failure, exact alternative comparison, and permission to run a three-session pilot.','P2','open','product-research','SRC-LOOTFLOW-95'),
('O-131','implementation','If revived, build an idempotent party-ledger fixture','Loot transfers can duplicate, disappear, leak permissions, or diverge after reconnect.','Use synthetic system-agnostic and D&D 5e items, pooled currency, claims, approvals, simultaneous edits, reconnect, undo, and audit history without publisher content.','No duplicate/lost transfer, deterministic conflict result, permission-safe claims, rollback, and portable unsupported-field report.','P2','open','runtime','SRC-LOOTFLOW-95'),
('O-132','research','Compare any revived LootFlow build with exact current loot/shop alternatives','The buyer may only need Item Piles, Quartermaster, a free chest, RPGX, The Stockpile, or a hosted campaign tool.','Run identical loot, shop, sell-back, and group-cart tasks and collect price choices and pilot commitments.','LootFlow wins a repeated failure rather than a visual preference and earns three non-zero price choices.','P2','open','product-research','SRC-LOOTFLOW-95'),
('O-133','research','Keep TurnReady rejected unless a qualified table names a repeated combat-focus failure','The broad action tracker and HUD surface is current-package crowded and the category payment signal belongs to incumbents.','Do not recruit or implement until a table reports an accessibility or interruption failure with the exact current stack and chooses a price test.','A named failure, exact alternative comparison, and permission to run a three-session pilot.','P2','open','product-research','SRC-TURNREADY-97'),
