('O-273','research','Run the No-Spoiler Player Return Brief price and alternative-choice test','Absent-player catch-up and stale campaign lore are plausible recurring pains, but the exact brief may be satisfied by a wiki, recap, assistant, or manual map/state update.','Recruit monthly/irregular/open/paid campaign GMs with a recent absence; compare normal recap, Archivist, Foundry Familiar, Campaign Codex, SessionFlow, LegendKeeper, shared fog, and the Return Brief at $10/$20/$39/no purchase.','7/10 repeated failures, 5/10 exact-brief preference, 3/10 non-zero choices, and two three-session pilots.','P0','open','product-research','SRC-RETURN-BRIEF-133'),
('O-274','implementation','Build a per-player spoiler and state-safety fixture for Return Brief','A recap can leak private facts, invent certainty, expose future content, or show stale character state.','Use two users, public/private facts, redaction, contradiction, revocation, stale links, absent-player map changes, actor deltas, GM approval, and acknowledgement in a disposable Foundry world.','No cross-player leakage, unknown/conflict preservation, deterministic revocation, authoritative reread, and an evidence-linked receipt.','P1','open','runtime','SRC-RETURN-BRIEF-133'),
('O-275','research','Define a user-owned content and privacy boundary for Return Brief','Recaps and lore may contain publisher text, protected art, player secrets, or data that should not leave the local world.','Store references, IDs, hashes, labels, approved text, audience, spoiler scope, and provenance; make cloud/AI processing opt-in and discard unapproved extracts.','No bundled publisher content, no hidden cloud retention, explicit user consent, and redaction before export.','P1','open','product-research','SRC-RETURN-BRIEF-133'),
('O-276','research','Test a neutral Return Brief manifest on a second VTT after Foundry proof','Roll20 and Owlbear differ in permissions, journal models, chat history, and player-state APIs.','Render a read-only preview from source references, audience, spoiler scope, timestamps, confidence, redactions, and unsupported mappings without claiming live parity.','One real second-VTT pilot, no copied rules/content, no hidden data, and visible unsupported states.','P2','open','runtime','SRC-RETURN-BRIEF-133'),
('O-277','research','Reopen Return Brief only for a named Foundry-local failure','Archivist, LegendKeeper, Tavern Scribe, Campaign Codex, SessionFlow, and manual recap/wiki workflows now cover the broad campaign-memory claim.','Recruit a table with a repeated local spoiler-safe re-entry failure that survives those exact alternatives, then record a direct price choice and pilot commitment.','Named failure, 5/10 exact-alternative preference, 3/10 non-zero prices, and one three-session pilot.','P2','open','product-research','SRC-RETURN-CORRECTION-134'),
('O-278','research','Run the World Doctor price and exact-alternative test','Update anxiety and recovery costs are strong, but GMs may prefer delaying updates, backups, hosting, or free/current tools.','Recruit long-running/module-heavy/paid/scheduled GMs; compare the same incident with the named alternatives and World Doctor at $15/$25/$39/no purchase.','7/10 named incidents, 5/10 exact-alternative preference, 3/10 non-zero choices, and two disposable-copy pilots.','P0','open','product-research','SRC-WORLD-DOCTOR-PAYER-135'),
('O-279','implementation','Build the World Doctor disposable-copy smoke-suite fixture','A preflight claim is unsafe unless it proves no live-world mutation and distinguishes package metadata from actual behavior.','Use a synthetic world and selected modules to exercise join, scene, permissions, roll, journal/macro, hook, and asset checks, then emit an evidence-linked receipt.','No live writes, deterministic report, authoritative reread, reversible restore, explicit unsupported state, and captured failure cases.','P0','open','runtime','SRC-WORLD-DOCTOR-PAYER-135'),
('O-280','research','Compare World Doctor with current Foundry and hosting alternatives','Foundry compatibility/versioning/backups, Find the Culprit, Quick Module Enable, Sephral, managed hosting, and duplicate-world practice may solve the real buyer job.','Show each alternative against the same recent incident and record time-to-decision, confidence, selected price, and pilot commitment.','Buyer chooses the rehearsal for a specific failure and pays or schedules the pilot.','P1','open','product-research','SRC-WORLD-DOCTOR-PAYER-135'),
('O-281','research','Test a second-VTT read-only World Doctor health receipt','Roll20 and Owlbear do not expose equivalent local migration and module surfaces.','Render a neutral receipt with package versions, test names, observations, unsupported mappings, and recovery references without claiming runtime parity.','One real second-VTT pilot, no copied rules/content, no hidden data, and visible unsupported states.','P2','open','runtime','SRC-WORLD-DOCTOR-PAYER-135'),
('O-282','research','Run the World Doctor price test only after a named incident','Category spending does not establish a buyer for a separate behavioral test runner.','Recruit a qualified GM with a recent failure or near miss; compare clone rehearsal with Foundry warnings, hosting, backups, culprit isolation, and duplicate-world practice at $15/$25/$39/no purchase.','Named incident, exact-alternative preference, 3 non-zero choices, and two disposable-copy pilots.','P1','open','product-research','SRC-WORLD-DOCTOR-CORRECTION-136'),
('O-283','implementation','Build the World Doctor behavioral smoke-suite fixture','A clone-based test must distinguish actual join/scene/permission/roll/journal/hook/asset behavior from package metadata without mutating the live world.','Use a synthetic world and explicit test names, run against a disposable copy, and emit evidence paths, unsupported states, authoritative reread, and recovery receipt.','No live writes, deterministic report, visible failure, reversible restore, and false-green cases captured.','P1','open','runtime','SRC-WORLD-DOCTOR-CORRECTION-136'),
('O-284','research','Run the Attendance-Resilient Side Session payer test','Home tables can cancel, ghost a character, or run a free one-shot; paid/professional tables may protect booked revenue and preparation.','Recruit paid/professional GMs, organized-play coordinators, and high-variance West Marches hosts; compare cancellation, free PDF, premium adventure, duplicate world, Oronder, and the capsule at $15/$30/$49/no purchase.','5/8 exact-alternative preference, 3/8 non-zero choices, quantified saved value, and two real pilots.','P0','open','product-research','SRC-MARKET-SCAN-137'),
('O-285','research','Audit current drop-in content and attendance competitors for the capsule test','Generic one-shots, interactive adventures, multi-world character tools, and session workspaces may already satisfy the job.','Compare Drop-in Dungeons, Prepared! 2, Dragonshorn, Boss Loot, Rultmoork, Omnipresence, Oronder, SessionFlow, and the buyer''s existing second-world workflow.','Named unsolved attendance failure and explicit reason the capsule is not merely another adventure or workspace.','P1','open','product-research','SRC-MARKET-SCAN-137'),
('O-286','implementation','Define a rights-safe portable capsule manifest','A cross-VTT offer can accidentally copy protected setting text, art, rules text, or hidden campaign state.','Separate original narrative/assets, neutral story/party/reward/recap references, and licensed system-specific stat blocks; show unsupported mappings on Roll20 or Owlbear.','Original or licensed assets only, no hidden data, stable IDs, attribution, and one read-only second-VTT preview.','P1','open','runtime','SRC-MARKET-SCAN-137'),
('O-287','research','Continue the wide ordinary-table search after the marketplace scan','No fresh broad utility category has yet beaten exact current packages and product-specific WTP.','Search recurring player/GM problems outside campaign memory, loot/trade, update safety, generic content, onboarding, mobile, scheduling, and combat HUDs; require a named payer and current competitor audit.','Fresh candidate, ordinary-table cohort, eye-catching message, exact alternatives, non-zero price, pilot, runtime, rights, and portability boundary.','P0','open','product-research','SRC-MARKET-SCAN-137'),
('O-288','research','Reopen a combat debrief only for a named repeated learning failure','Replay and analytics are already available and a second tool could be a novelty purchase.','Recruit combat-heavy tables with a recent rules-review or player-learning incident; compare Battle Replay, Combat Stats, Damage Log, PF2e Combater, native/system tools, and a player-safe debrief.','Named failure, exact-alternative rejection, 3 non-zero price choices, and two pilots.','P2','open','product-research','SRC-COMBAT-REPLAY-138'),
('O-289','implementation','Define a visibility-safe combat debrief event and correction receipt','Combat records can expose hidden enemies, GM-only rolls, private tactics, or irreversible state changes.','Use synthetic hidden/public actors and events to filter, replay, correct, and export only allowed information without rerunning or mutating the combat.','No hidden-state leakage, deterministic correction/redo, authoritative reread, and explicit unsupported events.','P2','open','runtime','SRC-COMBAT-REPLAY-138'),
('O-290','research','Continue fresh ordinary-table discovery beyond the current negative controls','Pass 138 closes another vivid but occupied category; no new broad payer winner has emerged.','Search recurring problems not represented by campaign memory, attendance, update safety, shops/loot, content, onboarding, mobile, scheduling, combat replay, HUD, or DMF automation.','Fresh payer, direct competitor audit, eye-catching message, non-zero price, pilot, runtime, rights, and portability evidence.','P0','open','product-research','SRC-COMBAT-REPLAY-138'),
('O-291','research','Run a current Player Compass residual-failure test','The current player-friction signal is strong but free/system controls may be good enough.','Recruit players and GMs with a repeated named failure after Player Pilot, Foundry Navigator, system HUDs, hidden tabs, and current builders; compare a read-only context explanation at $10/$20/$30/no purchase.','Named repeated failure, exact-alternative preference, 3 non-zero choices, and two real-table pilots.','P2','open','product-research','SRC-PLAYER-CORRECTION-139'),
('O-292','implementation','Build a player accessibility and capability-explanation fixture only if the residual test passes','System-specific actions, hidden state, focus, permissions, and reconnect behavior can make a generic cockpit unsafe or misleading.','Use synthetic D&D5e/PF2e actors and per-user visibility to test focus recovery, action explanation, unsupported states, reconnect, and native-sheet escape.','No hidden-state leakage, keyboard/screen-reader path, deterministic unsupported result, authoritative reread, and no live mutation.','P2','open','runtime','SRC-PLAYER-CORRECTION-139'),
('O-293','research','Run the Attendance-Resilient Side Session price and cohort gate','Home tables may prefer cancellation or a free side activity; paid/professional tables may protect booked value.','Recruit paid/professional GMs, organized-play coordinators, and West Marches hosts plus home-table controls; compare exact alternatives at $15/$30/$49/no purchase.','5/8 exact-alternative preference, 3/8 non-zero choices, quantified saved value, and two real pilots.','P0','open','product-research','SRC-ADAPTIVE-COMPETITION-140'),
('O-294','research','Run the full current competitor comparison for Attendance-Resilient Side Session','Existing adventure content, multi-world sync, Discord workflows, and session canvases may satisfy the same incident.','Use the same attendance incident with Drop-in Dungeons, Prepared! 2, Dragonshorn, Omnipresence, Oronder, SessionFlow, duplicate world, free PDF, and the capsule.','Named residual failure and explicit buyer reason not to use another adventure, sync tool, workspace, or manual workflow.','P1','open','product-research','SRC-ADAPTIVE-COMPETITION-140'),
('O-295','implementation','Define and test the rights-safe portable capsule manifest','Original narrative, art, rules references, stat blocks, hidden state, and reward exports have different rights and portability boundaries.','Separate original/licensed assets, neutral story/party/reward/recap data, and system adapters; preview unsupported mappings on Roll20 or Owlbear.','Stable IDs, attribution, no copied protected content, no hidden data, and one read-only second-VTT pilot.','P1','open','runtime','SRC-ADAPTIVE-COMPETITION-140'),
('O-296','research','Measure whether Attendance-Resilient is broad or professional-only','A product that sells only to paid GMs may be viable but does not meet the ordinary-table goal.','Compare conversion intent, price, saved value, and pilot commitment between home weekly groups, paid GMs, organized play, West Marches, and convention/event organizers.','Cohort-specific price choices, rejection reasons, repeat-use intent, and a documented market-size decision.','P0','open','product-research','SRC-ADAPTIVE-COMPETITION-140');

INSERT OR REPLACE INTO kb_trials(trial_id,area,symptom,attempted_approach,failure_cause,correction,evidence_status,source_id) VALUES
('T-073','market-selection','The fresh search found repeated update and maintenance anxiety among module-heavy Foundry campaigns.','Assume a compatibility dashboard or backup browser is a new product.','Core backups, recovery modules, asset auditing, culprit isolation, file tools, and packaging tools already cover adjacent jobs.','Keep World Doctor only as evidence-linked preflight plus disposable rehearsal and recovery receipt.','Current-competition correction recorded; buyer price, exact rehearsal, and portability remain pending.','SRC-WORLD-DOCTOR-73'),
('T-074','market-selection','World Doctor could be valuable but the buyer segment and price are not yet proven.','Assume every Foundry user will pay for update safety or launch a subscription.','Casual users can delay updates or use core backups; community pricing favors buy-once options; Roll20/Owlbear do not expose equivalent local migration surfaces.','Test qualified long-running/paid GMs at $15/$25/$39/no purchase and require a disposable-copy pilot before implementation.','Payer/boundary correction recorded; behavioral WTP, runtime, and second-VTT proof remain pending.','SRC-WORLD-DOCTOR-74'),
('T-075','market-selection','The fresh scan found direct consumer demand for better live drawing and a separate request for simple player trading.','Assume every visible request is a new product.','Item Piles already covers robust player trading, while mobile companion products cover simplified access; the remaining candidate with strong eye-catching value is live map annotation.','Open Tactical Sketchbook only as a fresh challenger and audit its exact drawing competitors before implementation.','Fresh challenger recorded; buyer choice, runtime, price, and portability remain pending.','SRC-SKETCHBOOK-75'),
('T-076','market-selection','Tactical Sketchbook initially looked like a broad unserved drawing category.','Sell a generic Excalidraw clone or drawing overhaul.','Foundry core, Precise Drawing Tools, Advanced Drawing Tools, Dungeon Draw, Quickdraw, Roll20, and a premium early-access direction cover broad drawing improvements.','Narrow the candidate to fast scoped live-play layers, temporary cleanup, snapshots, and native export.','Competition correction recorded; buyer price, pilot, and exact fixture remain pending.','SRC-SKETCHBOOK-76'),
('T-077','market-selection','Tactical Sketchbook has a clear demo and category price signal but no product-specific WTP.','Infer payment from an explicit community comment or premium competitor.','The buyer may prefer free modules, a separate whiteboard, or existing premium tools; portability is only a neutral-record hypothesis.','Test drawing-heavy GMs at $10/$20/$30/no purchase and require a three-session Foundry pilot before any cross-VTT or implementation claim.','Buyer/portability/marketing gate recorded; WTP, permission fixture, and adapter proof remain pending.','SRC-SKETCHBOOK-77'),
('T-078','market-selection','Tactical Sketchbook''s generic drawing promise survived only because a premium competitor was treated as future rather than current evidence.','Continue to treat â€œbetter drawingâ€ as an open product category.','Gambit''s Image Viewer already provides premium real-time media annotation and Enhanced Drawing targets premium canvas drawing; core and free modules cover more pieces.','Demote the broad category and retain only temporary scoped live-scene annotation for a later buyer test.','Current-package correction recorded; narrow buyer price, fixture, and portability remain pending.','SRC-SKETCHBOOK-78'),
('T-079','market-selection','A v14 GM report shows a concrete fifteen-minute journal lookup failure during play.','Assume a generic global search bar or campaign wiki is the product.','Search and Highlight, Simple SearchBar, Quick Insert, Monk''s Enhanced Journal, Campaign Codex, World & Campaign Builder, and AI tools cover broad search/organization.','Open Adventure Navigator only as deterministic active-scene context plus a short evidence-linked runbook.','Fresh challenger recorded; buyer choice, runtime, privacy, licensing, and portability remain pending.','SRC-ADVENTURE-NAV-79'),
('T-080','market-selection','Adventure Navigator looked broadly unserved after a single journal-search incident.','Sell full-text search, tags, linked journals, AI chat, or another journal skin.','Current maintained packages and free campaign tools cover those capabilities.','Require a repeatable context fixture in which the product finds the exact source, linked documents, and next action faster than current substitutes.','Direct-competition correction recorded; buyer price, pilot, and exact fixture remain pending.','SRC-ADVENTURE-NAV-80'),
('T-081','market-selection','Adventure Navigator has an eye-catching time-saved demo but no product-specific WTP or portability proof.','Infer payment from minutes saved or from the existence of AI/search products.','GMs may prefer free modules, PDF search, Campaign Codex, World & Campaign Builder, or AI copilots; publisher-content handling and cross-VTT semantics are distinct risks.','Test $15/$25/$39/no purchase, three-session pilot, local-only indexing, and one second-VTT read-only boundary only after Foundry proof.','Buyer/portability/licensing gate recorded; WTP, permission/index correctness, and adapter proof remain pending.','SRC-ADVENTURE-NAV-81'),
('T-082','runtime-selection','Adventure Navigator is statically feasible through Foundry''s JournalEntry links and permission model.','Treat documented API methods as proof that a safe product is complete.','Permission changes, stale IDs, ranking quality, reconnect/reindex behavior, publisher-content handling, and second-VTT semantics remain unverified.','Build only a disposable read-only permission/stale-index fixture after buyer choice; keep implementation and legal claims paused.','Technical/licensing/portability correction recorded; buyer WTP, fixture, and adapter proof remain pending.','SRC-ADVENTURE-NAV-82'),
('T-083','market-selection','The cross-candidate scorecard prioritizes Adventure Navigator but cannot select it.','Treat the newest candidate as marketable because its demo is clearer than the alternatives.','Adventure Navigator still lacks product-specific price choices, pilots, runtime fixture evidence, and second-VTT proof; World Doctor remains a separate arm.','Run buyer gates first and keep implementation paused until behavior clears the explicit go/no-go criteria.','Scorecard recorded; no product selected.','SRC-MARKET-SCORECARD-83'),
('T-084','market-selection','A fresh community scan found a clear complaint about slow improvised scene creation.','Assume a full map editor, asset browser, or import wizard is an open category.','MapForge, FA Nexus, Moulinette, Scene Express, Mass Import, and external map makers already cover broad map-authoring needs.','Open Rapid Encounter Board only as a temporary live-staging hypothesis and test it against the buyer''s current workflow.','Fresh challenger recorded; direct competition, price, runtime, and portability remain pending.','SRC-RAPID-SCENE-84'),
('T-085','market-selection','Rapid Encounter Board remains conditional after direct competition correction.','Infer marketability from the thirty-second demo or community frustration.','The category is crowded and the narrow staging wedge has no product-specific WTP, runtime fixture, or second-VTT proof.','Require a non-zero price, three-session pilot, disposable scope/promotion fixture, and one explicit portable package boundary before implementation.','Direct competition/portability correction recorded; no product selected.','SRC-RAPID-SCENE-85'),
('T-086','market-selection','MapForge''s Patreon access and buyer comments prove category payment signal but close the generic product gap.','Treat competitor adoption as evidence that a new map studio will also sell.','The visible payment signal belongs to MapForge, which already owns the generic in-Foundry studio promise.','Run Rapid Encounter Board only as a distinct temporary live-staging comparison with a non-zero price and pilot gate.','Marketability correction recorded; Rapid Encounter Board remains third and unselected.','SRC-RAPID-SCENE-86'),
('T-087','market-selection','A fresh scan found real but mixed pain around new and returning players using Foundry.','Assume a simplified player UI or mobile panel is a new market.','Hide UI, Player Pilot, core orientation, character builders, hero selection, ready checks, and premium player workspaces cover most broad requests.','Open TableStart only as a GM-authored per-scene session recipe and test a named onboarding/return-to-play incident at a non-zero price.','Fresh challenger recorded; buyer, runtime, portability, and licensing remain pending.','SRC-PLAYER-START-87'),
('T-088','market-selection','TableStart''s guided session recipe remains a narrow fourth candidate after competition correction.','Infer payment from player enthusiasm or from the existence of a polished first-action demo.','Current free and premium tools may be good enough, and players may adapt after one session.','Require head-to-head comparison, $10/$20/$30/no-purchase choice, three-session pilot, permission/reconnect fixture, and one adapter boundary before implementation.','Direct competition/payer correction recorded; no product selected.','SRC-PLAYER-START-88'),
('T-089','market-selection','A fresh scan found recurring multi-device coordination pain in in-person and hybrid Foundry play.','Assume a single integrated table mode is a new category because users assemble many modules and devices.','Monk''s Common Display, Physical Play Dice, TouchVTT, Player Pilot, Gaming Table, and related tools cover most visible components.','Open Tabletop Bridge only as an orchestration/setup-recovery challenger and require a cold-start task plus real-table pilot.','Fresh challenger recorded; buyer, runtime, portability, and price remain pending.','SRC-TABLETOP-89'),
('T-090','market-selection','Tabletop Bridge remains a narrow fifth candidate after direct competition correction.','Infer payment from high-engagement setup discussions or hardware ownership.','The current components are mostly free or separately supported, Ninjo''s In-Person Tools is a current integration anchor, and second-VTT parity is weak.','Require measurable setup/recovery savings, a $20/$35/$50/no-purchase choice, three-session pilot, secret-safe fixture, and one neutral adapter boundary.','Direct competition/marketability correction recorded; no product selected.','SRC-TABLETOP-90'),
('T-091','market-selection','Current v14 table-mode packages close the broad Tabletop Bridge feature gap.','Treat a multi-module in-person setup as evidence that a new integrated module will sell.','Ninjo''s In-Person Tools and Digital Tabletops are current; Table Mode is narrow/stale; no product-specific payment evidence is observed.','Park Tabletop Bridge and revive only for a paid reliability/orchestration failure that current packages cannot solve.','Current-package correction and demotion recorded; no product selected.','SRC-TABLETOP-91'),
('T-092','market-selection','Migration tooling shows stronger category payment evidence than recent feature candidates.','Assume importer Patreon access and historical R20Converter payments select a new product.','DDB-Importer, VTTA, R20Converter, PDF-to-Foundry, and scene migrators cover source-specific imports; migration is episodic.','Open VTT BridgeCheck only as a post-import assurance/repair receipt and test it against the exact importer plus manual cleanup.','Fresh challenger recorded; buyer, runtime, licensing, and portability remain pending.','SRC-BRIDGECHECK-92'),
('T-093','market-selection','VTT BridgeCheck remains conditional after direct competition and rights correction.','Build a generic cross-VTT converter or store imported publisher content.','Source-specific tools occupy import, source terms constrain access, and VTT semantics differ.','Require named post-import failure, non-zero one-time price, two campaign pilots, disposable safe rehearsal, no content copying, and one adapter boundary.','Direct competition/licensing/portability correction recorded; no product selected.','SRC-BRIDGECHECK-93'),
('T-094','market-selection','A fresh scan found recurring consumer-facing friction in loot, shops, and party treasury.','Assume a universal loot/shop/inventory surface is a new market.','Item Piles, Quartermaster, Backpack, RPGX, The Stockpile, and hosted campaign tools already cover the broad job.','Open LootFlow only as a narrow conflict-safe transaction-ledger hypothesis and compare it with the exact current stack.','Fresh challenger recorded; buyer price, pilot, runtime, and portability remain pending.','SRC-LOOTFLOW-94'),
('T-095','market-selection','LootFlow is rejected after the current-package and marketability correction.','Build a prettier shop or duplicate shared inventory, or infer product WTP from a community request.','The premium Stockpile already demonstrates the eye-catching group-cart/economy workflow, while free/current alternatives cover ordinary tables.','Keep only the neutral ledger idea as a reusable asset and require named repeated failure, non-zero price, and three-session pilot before revival.','Direct competition/demotion recorded; no product selected.','SRC-LOOTFLOW-95'),
('T-096','market-selection','A fresh scan found recurring consumer-facing friction in combat action budgets.','Assume a universal action/reaction tracker is a new market.','Action Keeper, Reaction Tracker, current HUDs, system-native tools, and combat advisors already cover much of the job.','Open TurnReady only as a minimal private accessibility/turn-focus hypothesis and compare it with the exact current stack.','Fresh challenger recorded; buyer price, pilot, runtime, and portability remain pending.','SRC-TURNREADY-96'),
('T-097','market-selection','TurnReady is rejected after the current-package, payment, and portability correction.','Build another action HUD, generic rules engine, or infer product WTP from category incumbents.','A paid HUD proves category spending, not a new product; system action semantics and write permissions make portability nontrivial.','Keep only the neutral action-ledger idea as a reusable asset and require named accessibility/interruption failure, non-zero price, and three-session pilot before revival.','Direct competition/demotion recorded; no product selected.','SRC-TURNREADY-97'),
('T-098','market-selection','The current shortlist needs an evidence-weighted buyer-test order, not another unranked feature idea.','Promote the newest or most visually impressive candidate, or transfer category payment from one product to another.','Only VTT BridgeCheck has the strongest combined payment proxy and high-intent deadline signal; it still needs exact-importer comparison.','Run BridgeCheck first, then World Doctor, Adventure Navigator, Rapid Encounter Board, and TableStart with separate gates; keep negative controls parked.','Sequencing correction recorded; no product selected.','SRC-SCORECARD-98'),
('T-099','runtime-selection','Foundry local data and package/backup metadata support a narrower BridgeCheck fixture.','Build a generic importer that accesses DDB credentials, mutates live worlds, or treats backups as complete asset coverage.','Use read-only disposable Foundry inputs, verify assets/links/ownership/version metadata, and retain receipt evidence only.','Technical/rights boundary recorded; fixture, buyer WTP, and exact-importer comparison remain pending.','Technical boundary recorded; fixture and buyer proof remain pending.','SRC-BRIDGECHECK-99'),
('T-100','portability-selection','Cross-VTT parity is not credible from current official surfaces.','Promise a universal Roll20/DDB/Owlbear converter or directly access user accounts.','Retain a portable receipt contract; defer user-mediated Roll20 and compact Owlbear adapters until Foundry buyer/runtime proof.','Portability correction recorded; no product selected.','Portability boundary recorded; Foundry proof and one adapter test remain pending.','SRC-BRIDGECHECK-100'),
('T-101','market-selection','A fresh recurring player-friction scan found persistent confusion but current HUD competition is strong.','Build another action bar or sheet replacement because players report tabs and icons as confusing.','Open Player Compass only as automatic context selection plus plain-language explanation, then compare it with exact HUD and orientation controls.','Fresh challenger recorded; buyer WTP, three-session pilot, read-only fixture, and second-VTT boundary remain pending.','Fresh challenger recorded; no product selected.','SRC-PLAYER-COMPASS-101'),
('T-102','market-selection','The payer scan found recurring premium UX spending but no product-specific WTP.','Keep BridgeCheck first solely because its migration urgency and importer payment proxy look stronger.','Move Player Compass first for a separate buyer gate while retaining BridgeCheck second; do not transfer premium HUD payment to the new wedge.','Sequencing correction recorded; exact buyer choice, pilots, runtime, and portability remain pending.','Sequencing correction recorded; no product selected.','SRC-SCORECARD-102'),
('T-103','market-selection','Public users pay for and praise a direct HUD incumbent, but some reject visual overload and subscriptions.','Treat incumbent satisfaction as proof that any new player surface will sell.','Incumbent payment and satisfaction may come from visual presentation, support, or direct actions rather than the Player Compass wedge.','Use minimal mode, one-time pricing, exact-feature attribution, and a no-purchase control before advancing Player Compass.','Behavioral payment signal recorded; Player Compass WTP and pilot remain pending.','SRC-PAYER-SIGNAL-103'),
('T-104','market-selection','A fresh scan found repeated target-resolution friction with a visible one-click confirmation wedge.','Build a generic combat automation engine or bypass Foundry permissions so players can mutate enemy actors directly.','Current substitutes are system-specific and free; the safer gap is a target-aware, GM-authorized handoff with explicit expiry, adjustment, and undo.','Open Resolve Relay as a seventh conditional challenger and require exact-stack preference, one-time price, pilot, safe fixture, and one later adapter boundary.','Fresh challenger recorded; no product selected.','SRC-RESOLVE-RELAY-104'),
('T-105','market-selection','The exact-package check weakened the proposed Resolve Relay paid gap.','Treat useful target-aware combat handoff behavior as proof of a new paid product.','Current PF2e Toolbelt, PF2e Saves Helper, and Effective Tray NG cover most of the workflow; premium automation payment is only category evidence.','Demote Resolve Relay to a negative control and preserve its intent-envelope, stale, and undo patterns as reusable assets.','Direct-payment correction recorded; no product selected.','SRC-RESOLVE-RELAY-105'),
('T-106','market-selection','A fresh scan found recurring self-hosting and player-join failures with paid hosting anchors.','Build another generic tunnel or assume hosting payment transfers to a local utility.','Free tunnels and tunnel managers solve pieces, while Molten and The Forge solve managed hosting; the gap is provider-neutral reliability, verification, reconnect, and safe fallback.','Open TableLink as the next fresh conditional challenger and require exact free/paid comparison, price choices, multi-session pilot, runtime fixture, and security boundary.','Fresh challenger recorded; no product selected.','SRC-TABLELINK-106'),
('T-107','market-selection','The exact competitor pass found that Foundry Tunnel Manager closes the generic TableLink gateway claim.','Treat a Windows tunnel wrapper, provider selector, dashboard, or tunnel notification as a new paid product.','FTM already provides those capabilities; the remaining hypothesis is a pre-session independent invite verifier and minimal health receipt.','Demote generic TableLink, open JoinProof as the next challenger, and require FTM/manual/host comparison plus external-probe, price, pilot, runtime, privacy, and portability gates.','Direct-competition correction recorded; no product selected.','SRC-JOINPROOF-107'),
('T-108','market-selection','Foundry core and generic monitoring close most of the JoinProof external-verification claim.','Assume a remote URL checker is a new Foundry product.','Foundry remote check, UptimeRobot, Uptime Kuma, FTM, and a phone or player test cover basic reachability; semantic session verification remains unproven.','Park JoinProof and retain only false-green, stale-session, and health-receipt assets until a named failure and price choice appear.','External-verification correction recorded; no product selected.','SRC-JOINPROOF-108'),
('T-109','market-selection','A fresh scan found recurring campaign quorum and cancellation pain with strong external competition.','Build another poll, calendar, or RSVP screen.','Doodle, Discord Events, Warhorn, Foundry, Campaign Builder, and SessionFlow cover broad scheduling or session planning.','Open Session Pulse only as consequence-aware quorum and fallback; require exact-stack preference, non-zero price, three-cycle pilot, privacy fixture, and portable event contract.','Fresh challenger recorded; no product selected.','SRC-SESSION-PULSE-109'),
('T-110','market-selection','Doodle payment establishes a coordination category anchor but not Session Pulse conversion.','Treat Doodle Professional subscription and reminder features as proof that D&D GMs will pay.','Ordinary groups may use Doodle free, Discord, or messages; only a named prep-loss incident and exact-stack preference can transfer the signal.','Retain Session Pulse conditionally, separate payer segments, and require buy-once plus maintenance price tests and three real cycles.','Payer/price correction recorded; no product selected.','SRC-SESSION-PULSE-110'),
('T-111','market-selection','A fresh scan found substantial recurring GM prep burden but broad prep competition.','Open another prep canvas, AI generator, or scheduling product because users report long preparation and wasted work.','SessionFlow, World & Campaign Builder, RPGM Forge, current AI/prep tools, and premium content cover broad preparation; only safe reuse after a player pivot remains a possible gap.','Rerank existing candidates, keep generic prep as a negative control, and require a named pivot incident plus price and pilot evidence before opening a new product.','Scorecard/rerank correction recorded; no product selected.','SRC-SCORECARD-111'),
('T-112','runtime-selection','Current HUD and accessibility competitors close the broad Player Compass promise, and D&D5e/PF2e rights and semantics differ.','Treat package descriptions, incumbent payment, or a shared action model as proof of a safe portable product.','Foundry Navigator, Token Action HUD D&D5e, and PF2e HUD cover much of direct action access; system, content, art, permission, and accessibility boundaries remain adapter-specific.','Keep Player Compass as a narrow first buyer gate for read-only context explanation; require exact-HUD preference, separate synthetic fixtures, rights audit, and a later manifest-only second-VTT test.','Technical/licensing/portability correction recorded; no product selected.','SRC-PLAYER-COMPASS-112'),
('T-113','market-selection','Version fragmentation and upgrade anxiety are a strong consumer-GM problem, but official portable installs and managed hosts are close substitutes.','Open a generic compatibility dashboard, backup browser, or Foundry launcher as a paid product.','Foundry supports multiple portable versions, The Forge supports per-game versions, Molten supplies backups, and existing modules cover compatibility hints and diagnosis.','Open Campaign Anchor only as a campaign-specific environment lock with clone-before-upgrade, known-good launch, rollback receipt, and exact-alternative buyer test.','Fresh challenger recorded; no product selected.','SRC-CAMPAIGN-ANCHOR-113'),
('T-114','market-selection','Foundry core now covers most Campaign Anchor backup, snapshot, restore, and version-pinning promise.','Treat upgrade anxiety or hosting payment as proof that another local backup/version utility will sell.','Foundry backups and portable installs, managed hosts, and document-level recovery are strong substitutes; only an evidence-linked environment receipt remains distinct.','Demote Campaign Anchor to a conditional comparison arm and continue the fresh search; reopen only for a named failure that survives exact controls.','Direct-competition correction recorded; no product selected.','SRC-CAMPAIGN-ANCHOR-114'),
('T-115','market-selection','A fresh D&D5e 2024 downtime/Bastion scan found recurring between-session interest but a crowded package category.','Open a generic Bastion or downtime tracker because players want more to do between sessions.','Indy Ventures, Downtime 5e, Downtime Manager, Yugen, Universal Downtime Engine, Morelord, the official Bastion UI, and spreadsheets cover most broad workflows.','Park the candidate; retain player submission, GM approval, reconciliation, receipt, and portable project-state concepts for a named failure and buyer test.','Fresh challenger/competition correction recorded; no product selected.','SRC-BETWEEN-SESSIONS-115'),
('T-116','market-selection','A fresh scan found recurring session-zero expectation and campaign-fit pain.','Assume a private agreement wizard is automatically marketable because session-zero discussions are popular.','Safety Tools, Safety and Communication, Consent Form, forms, checklists, and direct conversation are strong substitutes; social/privacy harm is a material risk.','Keep Table Pact conditional and test only private answers, aggregate conflicts, versioned acknowledgements, re-checks, exact-alternative preference, and non-zero price.','Fresh challenger recorded; no product selected.','SRC-TABLE-PACT-116'),
('T-117','market-selection','A fresh scan found ammunition/resource-friction pain but strong opt-out behavior and current controls.','Build a generic resource tracker because players complain about counting arrows or supplies.','Ammo Tracker, RC Spent, Weapon Reload, Party Resources, Custom Fields, Bag o'' Lists, native quantities, macros, and hand-waving cover most demand; ordinary tables often reject the mechanic.','Reject broad Resource Steward; retain neutral resource-event and receipt patterns for a narrow survival-focused buyer test.','Fresh negative control recorded; no product selected.','SRC-RESOURCE-STEWARD-117'),
('T-118','market-selection','A fresh scan found audit/provenance pain for some long-running or open tables.','Build a generic character audit and rollback tool because a community comment requests one.','Character Tracker and yugen-tracker already cover broad audit, history, alerts, exports, and delivery; privacy and accusation risks are material.','Reject broad Character Integrity Ledger; retain redacted change events, role filtering, retention, and no-accusation UX for a named-incident test only.','Fresh negative control recorded; no product selected.','SRC-CHARACTER-INTEGRITY-118'),
('T-119','market-selection','A fresh scan found strong hybrid/mobile pain and genuine payment signals.','Build a generic mobile Foundry client because groups want character sheets on phones.','Foundry Tabletop Helpers, Swipe VTT, VTT Companion, PocketScroll, Diecast, Sheet Only, Mobile Improvements, and system-specific companions already cover the broad demo; sync, auth, app-store, and version-drift risks are material.','Open Player Pocket only as a narrow portable player-action contract and require exact-alternative preference, one-time price, multi-session two-device pilot, privacy, and second-VTT boundary.','Fresh conditional challenger recorded; no product selected.','SRC-PLAYER-POCKET-119'),
('T-120','market-selection','The exact mobile audit found the broad Player Pocket category is occupied across Foundry and other VTT ecosystems.','Treat incumbent mobile payment and a Foundry mobile gap as proof that a new cross-VTT adapter will sell.','PocketScroll, Swipe, VTT Companion, Diecast, Roll20 Characters, and D&D Beyond cover current mobile sheets/actions; adapter maintenance, auth, system differences, and two-VTT WTP remain unproven.','Demote the broad concept; reopen only for a named cross-VTT failure and a two-VTT one-time-price pilot using thin adapters.','Direct-competition and portability correction recorded; no product selected.','SRC-PLAYER-POCKET-120'),
('T-121','market-selection','A fresh scan found encounter-fit pain but a crowded builder and analytics category.','Build another monster generator or CR calculator because GMs report fights that miss the real party.','Encounter Forge, Giffyglyph''s Monster Maker, D&D Beyond Encounter Builder, Combat Stats, Battle Replay, Encounter Stats, and Grim Arithmetic cover generation, calibration, analytics, or simulation.','Open only Encounter Tuner: post-combat planned-versus-observed debrief plus explainable next-fight suggestions; require exact-alternative preference, non-zero price, three-session use, and neutral event portability.','Conditional challenger recorded; no product selected.','SRC-ENCOUNTER-TUNER-121'),
('T-122','market-selection','A fresh map-prep scan found an eye-catching readiness promise but strong exporter/importer competition.','Build another map creator or infer QA WTP from Dungeon Alchemist and Dungeondraft sales.','Universal Battlemap Importer, Dungeon Alchemist, Dungeondraft, MapForge, Mass Import, level import, and map splitting cover most setup; the remaining QA wedge overlaps BridgeCheck/World Doctor.','Reject SceneReady for now; retain readiness receipts, diffs, missing-asset reports, and neutral scene contracts as reusable assets.','Fresh negative control and direct-competition correction recorded; no product selected.','SRC-SCENEREADY-122'),
('T-123','market-selection','A fresh scan found a high-urgency blocked-player incident but a narrow and technically expensive fallback category.','Build a generic mobile VTT or assume a device complaint proves a broad paid market.','Foundry requirements and iPad limitations establish the incident; Performance Optimizer, Swipe, foundry-mobile-companion, Foundry Lightweight Client, screen sharing, and switching VTTs are direct alternatives.','Open only CanvasBridge: a canvasless, permission-scoped player relay for a named excluded player; require exact-alternative preference, one-time WTP, two-session retention, and neutral player-session portability.','Conditional challenger recorded; no product selected.','SRC-CANVASBRIDGE-123'),
('T-124','market-selection','The current-package audit found that CanvasBridge overlaps a mature mobile and lightweight-client category.','Treat a device-exclusion incident as proof that a new general relay or mobile sheet will sell.','D&D5e Mobile Companion, Companion Bridge/VTT Companion, Foundry Mobile Companion, Foundry Lightweight Client, performance profiles, and screen sharing cover the ordinary fallback job.','Demote CanvasBridge to a negative control; reopen only for a named residual failure that survives every exact alternative and yields non-zero one-time WTP plus a two-session pilot.','Direct-competition and payer correction recorded; no product selected.','SRC-CANVASBRIDGE-124'),
('T-125','market-selection','The fresh search found real prepared-spell loadout demand.','Assume a full character-kit utility is new because players want context-specific presets.','D&D5e Spell Book and PF2e Prepper already provide named spell loadouts, while native and system-specific controls cover adjacent state and frequency is uneven.','Reject the generic Loadout Compass; retain only an explicit reversible full-kit boundary for a named non-spell failure and direct WTP.','Direct-competition/demotion recorded; no product selected.','SRC-LOADOUT-COMPASS-125'),
('T-126','market-selection','The fresh search found a vivid GM-time request for player-applied damage under a trust toggle.','Assume a broad delegated-action permission layer is a new paid product.','Effective Tray NG, Midi-QoL, Damage Application, Always HP, and D&D5e damage prompts already cover much of the D&D5e case; cross-system authority is risky and unproven.','Reject the broad Trusted Table product; retain only a neutral audited action envelope for a qualified multi-system/accessibility failure.','Direct-competition/safety correction recorded; no product selected.','SRC-TRUSTED-TABLE-126'),
('T-127','market-selection','The fresh reset found stronger explicit payment language for an Excalidraw-like live layer but no distinct winner.','Invent a new product name or treat a category payment signal as proof of a new product.','Whiteboard Experience, core/advanced drawing, Dungeon Draw, and Gambit cover the broad space; the remaining narrow workflow is already Tactical Sketchbook.','Keep Tactical Sketchbook conditional, keep Player Compass first in buyer testing, and continue the wide search with Dungeon Master''s Forge backburnered.','Fresh-search reset recorded; no product selected.','SRC-FRESH-RESET-127'),
('T-128','market-selection','A fresh current-package scan found that player guidance, onboarding, mobile access, and performance are more occupied than the prior audit recorded.','Open a generic Player Compass, teach-players wizard, FPS dashboard, or low-spec/mobile product from a category wish or a polished demo.','Foundry Navigator, Character Builder, Player Orientation, Prime Performance, Geano''s Scene Optimizer, and Swipe VTT cover the broad claims; only named residual incidents remain plausible.','Keep only named-incident conditional arms, require exact-stack rejection and product-specific WTP/pilots, and continue the wide search with Dungeon Master''s Forge backburnered.','Current-package correction recorded; no product selected.','SRC-PACKAGE-RESET-128'),
('T-129','market-selection','A fresh community scan found vivid hybrid-display and GM-scratchpad requests but no new product.','Build a generic shared-TV controller or sidebar notebook because the demos are easy to show.','Monk''s Common Display, Stage Master, Sheet Only, Physical Play Dice, Notebook, GM Screen, and Campaign Codex already occupy the ordinary workflows.','Reject the generic products; reopen only a cross-VTT private/shared handoff failure with exact-alternative rejection, price, pilots, and reconnect/privacy proof.','Fresh negative-control/current-competition correction recorded; no product selected.','SRC-HYBRID-SCRATCHPAD-129'),
('T-130','market-selection','A fresh scan found explicit creator payment intent for a polished live broadcast overlay but no ordinary-table product.','Transfer streamer willingness to pay into a general overlay product or build a new actor/stats dashboard.','Foundry Stream Overlay Free/Pro, OBS Utils, Stream View, Stream Utils, and adjacent overlays already cover the main broadcast workflows; consent, hidden-state, rights, and system mapping add maintenance cost.','Reject the generic creator product; retain a read-only broadcast packet and test only with qualified creators at a non-zero price and on a second VTT.','Creator-market negative control recorded; no ordinary-table product selected.','SRC-BROADCAST-OVERLAY-130'),
('T-131','market-selection','A fresh scan found a current zero-prep/minimum-configuration request and a plausible session-orchestration gap.','Assume a one-click session capsule is new because it looks more convenient than manual setup.','Dungeon Flow, Morelord Encounters, Encounter Forge, Mass Import, importer packages, premium adventures, Adventure Navigator, TableStart, and Rapid Encounter Board cover major pieces; bundle economics and cross-VTT semantics are unproven.','Open Zero-Prep Session Capsule only as a low-priority conditional challenger and require exact buyer preference, non-zero WTP, pilots, Foundry safety, rights, and second-VTT proof.','Fresh conditional challenger recorded; no product selected.','SRC-ZERO-PREP-CAPSULE-131'),
('T-132','market-selection','The direct incumbent audit found the broad Zero-Prep Session Capsule overlaps a current premium session workspace.','Treat a one-canvas session workspace, import, or paid adventure as proof that a new capsule will sell.','SessionFlow, Dungeon Flow, paid content, and duplicate-world practice cover most broad paths; only a disposable player-safe transaction wrapper remains distinct and its WTP is unproven.','Demote the broad capsule and continue the fresh ordinary-table search; reopen only for a named transaction failure that survives exact alternatives.','Direct-incumbent correction recorded; no product selected.','SRC-ZERO-PREP-CORRECTION-132'),
('T-133','market-selection','A fresh scan found recurring absent-player and stale-lore pain in monthly and irregular campaigns.','Build a generic campaign wiki, transcript, or AI recap assistant.','Archivist Sync, Foundry Familiar, Campaign Codex, SessionFlow, LegendKeeper, native shared fog, and manual recap workflows cover broad recall, organization, assistant, and map claims.','Open No-Spoiler Player Return Brief only as a per-player, GM-approved, spoiler-scoped re-entry workflow and require direct WTP, exact-alternative preference, pilots, privacy, rights, and second-VTT manifest proof.','Fresh conditional challenger recorded; no product selected.','SRC-RETURN-BRIEF-133'),
('T-134','market-selection','Direct pricing and feature evidence showed that campaign-memory is already a paid incumbent category.','Treat a no-spoiler return card as a new standalone product because absent-player pain is vivid.','Archivist, LegendKeeper, and Tavern Scribe cover paid recap, permissions, secrets, player memory, and missed-session catch-up.','Demote the broad Return Brief, retain only permission/revocation records as reusable assets, and reopen only for a named Foundry-local failure with price and pilot evidence.','Direct payment/incumbent correction recorded; no product selected.','SRC-RETURN-CORRECTION-134'),
('T-135','market-selection','World Doctor has a high-consequence payer anchor but faces a strong current recovery and compatibility stack.','Build another backup browser, compatibility dashboard, or live-world repair tool from update anxiety.','Foundry core, Find the Culprit, Quick Module Enable, Sephral, hosting, and duplicate-world practice cover adjacent jobs; actual rehearsal safety and product-specific WTP remain unproven.','Move World Doctor to the first empirical gate: test $15/$25/$39/no purchase, exact alternatives, disposable-copy pilots, no-live mutation, rights/privacy, and a second-VTT receipt.','Payer-anchor/current-competition correction recorded; no product selected.','SRC-WORLD-DOCTOR-PAYER-135'),
('T-136','market-selection','The current incumbent and payer audit closed the broad World Doctor claim.','Treat Foundry warnings, backups, hosting, and category maintenance spending as proof that a new test runner will sell.','Foundry core, Molten, VTT Online, The Forge, and duplicate-world workflows cover metadata, recovery, or testing alternatives; only clone-based behavioral smoke testing remains distinct.','Demote World Doctor to a conditional comparison arm and require a named incident, exact-alternative preference, price choice, disposable-copy pilots, runtime safety, and portability receipt.','Direct-incumbent/payer correction recorded; no product selected.','SRC-WORLD-DOCTOR-CORRECTION-136'),
('T-137','market-selection','The fresh marketplace scan found strong content and professional-session payment but no new broad utility winner.','Build a generic loot/shop/inventory module or another ready-made one-shot because current category spending is visible.','Current shop, merchant, trading, crafting, loot, and premium adventure packages occupy those claims; the remaining attendance lead has measurable ROI only for paid/professional or high-variance organizers.','Run Attendance-Resilient Side Session as a bounded payer test with home tables as a negative control, then continue the wide ordinary-table search if it fails.','Fresh marketplace/ordinary-buyer correction recorded; no product selected.','SRC-MARKET-SCAN-137'),
('T-138','market-selection','A fresh scan found a vivid combat-replay/debrief demo but current packages already cover the broad promise.','Build another battle recorder, analytics dashboard, or undo tool from replay and correction requests.','Battle Replay, Combat Stats, Damage Log, PF2e Combater, screen recording, system debuggers, and native workflows cover replay, analytics, correction, or review.','Reject the generic product; retain event/timeline/visibility/correction/export assets and reopen only for a named learning failure with price and pilots.','Combat replay negative-control correction recorded; no product selected.','SRC-COMBAT-REPLAY-138'),
('T-139','market-selection','A current high-engagement player-friction thread did not establish a new paid cockpit or character product.','Build another player HUD, mobile panel, character creator, or source allowlist because players report confusion.','Player Pilot, Foundry Navigator, system HUDs, hidden tabs, tutorials, D&D5e Character Builder, and D&D Character Creator cover the broad workflow.','Keep Player Compass conditional only for a named residual failure and require exact-alternative rejection, price, accessibility/runtime proof, and pilots.','Current player-friction/character-source correction recorded; no product selected.','SRC-PLAYER-CORRECTION-139'),
('T-140','market-selection','The current competitor audit left a narrow attendance-resilient content-plus-workflow boundary but no market validation.','Sell another one-shot, map pack, campaign workspace, or multi-world sync feature as the answer to an absent-player night.','Drop-in Dungeons, Prepared! 2, Dragonshorn, Omnipresence, Oronder, SessionFlow, and premium cinematic adventures cover broad components; only no-canon variable-party safe exit remains distinct.','Run the paid/professional cohort price and competitor gate with home tables as a negative control, then continue the ordinary-table search if it proves niche-only.','Adaptive competitor/payer/portability correction recorded; no product selected.','SRC-ADAPTIVE-COMPETITION-140');

INSERT OR REPLACE INTO kb_metadata(key,value) VALUES
('research_status_current','#1-#142 complete as research passes; Audio Secrets / Scene Sound Director is a fresh conditional comparison arm after a current per-player-audio scan; premium audio payment does not prove routing-product WTP; Attendance-Resilient Side Session remains the first bounded payer gate; Dungeon Master''s Forge remains backburnered; no product selected');

INSERT OR REPLACE INTO kb_sources(source_id,title,source_kind,scope,authority,status,location,captured_at,version_fingerprint,notes) VALUES
('SRC-SELECTIVE-AUDIO-141','Selective audio / private-scene-sound fresh lead','project','project','Current per-player audio request, Foundry playlist and audio API documentation, and current package pages','active','..\\PRODUCT_RESEARCH.md','2026-09-26','141 selective-audio/private-scene-sound/competition/payer/portability pass','Audio Secrets is a conditional buyer gate; no product selected and Dungeon Master''s Forge remains backburnered'),
('SRC-AUDIO-CORRECTION-142','Selective audio direct-incumbent and payer correction','project','project','Current premium audio packages, Patreon audio monetization, recipient macros, Token Audio FX, Playlist Plus, and private-audio community evidence','active','..\\PRODUCT_RESEARCH.md','2026-09-26','142 audio-routing/direct-competition/payer/rights/portability correction pass','Category audio payment is not routing-product WTP; test qualified audio-heavy cohorts separately');

INSERT OR REPLACE INTO kb_facts(fact_id,domain,subject_no,title,statement,scope,evidence_class,status,source_id,tags) VALUES
('F-613','buyer-pain','', 'Per-player audio is a current concrete Foundry pain','A current community request asks for a playlist or boombox that only one player hears and reports that ambient-radius workarounds do not express player identity or level/zone semantics cleanly. This is recruiting evidence, not payment evidence.','project','static','provisional','SRC-SELECTIVE-AUDIO-141','buyer-pain,audio,private,players,scene,region,recruiting'),
('F-614','competition','', 'Foundry playlists are global but recipient-aware audio can be scripted','Core playlists broadcast globally, while the current Foundry audio API can accept explicit recipients. The gap is reliable, discoverable workflow rather than raw runtime impossibility.','project','static','provisional','SRC-SELECTIVE-AUDIO-141','competition,foundry,playlist,audio-api,recipients,macro'),
('F-615','competition','', 'Current modules occupy pieces of selective audio','Chris Sound Module exposes a specific-player macro but is only verified through Foundry 12; Token Audio FX supports owner-scoped one-shot playback; Enhanced Region Behavior triggers sound/music from regions; Playlist Plus and Narrator''s Jukebox occupy general audio control.','project','static','provisional','SRC-SELECTIVE-AUDIO-141','competition,chris-sound,token-sounds,regions,playlist-plus,narrator-jukebox'),
('F-616','market-product-boundary','', 'Audio Secrets is a recipient/scene/queue layer, not another jukebox','The candidate routes user-owned audio to named players, party subsets, token owners, or scene/region conditions; supports queue/loop/private preview; and shows expected recipients without bundling copyrighted music or replacing general playlist management.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-SELECTIVE-AUDIO-141','product-boundary,audio-secrets,recipients,queue,preview,rights'),
('F-617','buyer-pain','', 'The strongest payer hypothesis is audio-heavy paid or professional play','Horror, investigation, narrative, actual-play, organized-play, and paid/professional GMs may value private clues and location-specific sound; home weekly groups are a required negative control because macros, voice chat, or headphones may be sufficient.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-SELECTIVE-AUDIO-141','buyer-pain,paid-gm,professional,horror,investigation,negative-control'),
('F-618','marketability','', 'Selective audio has a legible eye-catching demo','â€œThe rogue hears the whisper; the rest of the party hears the roomâ€ demonstrates recipient routing immediately with a live player/zone preview, making the value clearer than a generic audio-settings panel.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-SELECTIVE-AUDIO-141','marketability,demo,audio,whisper,zone,private'),
('F-619','portability-rights','', 'Selective audio portability requires a neutral route manifest','The portable artifact can contain user-owned asset references, recipient scope, trigger/zone, queue policy, duration, and unsupported fields. Foundry is first; Roll20 or Owlbear begins as a read-only preview.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-SELECTIVE-AUDIO-141','portability,rights,manifest,roll20,owlbear,user-owned'),
('F-620','market-selection','', 'Audio Secrets has no product-specific WTP after the first direct audit','Premium audio packages prove category spending, but routing can be scripted and current modules cover pieces. Advance only after a named repeated incident, exact-alternative rejection, a non-zero one-time price, two pilots, and privacy/rights/runtime proof.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-AUDIO-CORRECTION-142','market-selection,audio-secrets,wtp,pilot,privacy,rights,no-product-selected');

INSERT OR REPLACE INTO kb_decisions(decision_id,topic,decision,rationale,scope,status,owner,source_id,next_review) VALUES
('D-257','market-selection','Open Audio Secrets / Scene Sound Director only as a fresh conditional buyer gate.','The per-player audio incident is concrete and visually demonstrable, but current APIs and modules cover pieces of the job.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-SELECTIVE-AUDIO-141',NULL),
('D-258','market-product-boundary','Constrain Audio Secrets to recipient, scene, and queue semantics over user-owned audio.','A new jukebox, soundboard, music pack, or general audio dashboard would duplicate current tools and increase rights/support scope.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-SELECTIVE-AUDIO-141',NULL),
('D-259','market-selection','Test audio-heavy paid/professional and horror/investigation cohorts separately from home groups.','The payer may be a narrow professional or immersion-focused segment; home tables are a negative control and WTP cannot transfer between cohorts.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-AUDIO-CORRECTION-142',NULL),
('D-260','portability-rights','Use a neutral audio-route manifest and user-owned media boundary.','Recipient, trigger, queue, duration, and unsupported fields can travel, while audio content, account access, and VTT runtime semantics should not be copied or impersonated.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-SELECTIVE-AUDIO-141',NULL),
('D-261','market-selection','Do not infer selective-audio WTP from premium music or jukebox subscriptions.','Those payments may buy content, curation, polish, or maintenance rather than recipient routing.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-AUDIO-CORRECTION-142',NULL),
('D-262','market-selection','Continue the ordinary-table search if Audio Secrets proves professional-only.','A viable niche product would not satisfy the broad ordinary-table objective without broader cohort evidence.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-AUDIO-CORRECTION-142',NULL);

INSERT OR REPLACE INTO kb_open_items(item_id,item_class,title,problem,next_action,evidence_needed,priority,status,owner,source_id) VALUES
('O-297','research','Run the Audio Secrets buyer-price and exact-alternative gate','Per-player audio interest may be satisfied by a macro, region, or current audio module and the payer may be narrow.','Recruit qualified audio-heavy GMs and home controls; show the same private/subset audio incident through exact alternatives at $10/$20/$30/no purchase.','5/8 qualified preference, 3/8 non-zero choices, two three-session pilots, and coded rejection reasons.','P1','open','product-research','SRC-AUDIO-CORRECTION-142'),
('O-298','research','Compare Audio Secrets against recipient macros and current audio packages','A polished UI may add no value if a macro or Playlist Plus already solves the incident.','Run the same recipient/scene/queue task with core playlists, a recipient macro, Chris Sound Module, Token Audio FX, Enhanced Region Behavior, Playlist Plus, and Audio Secrets.','Named repeated failure and explicit reason not to use each exact alternative.','P1','open','product-research','SRC-SELECTIVE-AUDIO-141'),
('O-299','implementation','Build a synthetic two-client selective-audio fixture only after the buyer gate','Recipient changes, reconnect, late join, region entry, and hidden routes can leak audio or create stale playback.','Use synthetic user-owned tracks and two players to test private preview, route changes, queues, loops, ownership, reconnect, and audit receipts.','No unintended recipients, no path disclosure, deterministic reconnect, and no live mutation beyond route state.','P1','open','runtime','SRC-SELECTIVE-AUDIO-141'),
('O-300','implementation','Define the rights-safe audio-route manifest','Bundled music, hosted audio, or account integration could create licensing and privacy obligations.','Separate user-owned asset references from recipient/trigger/queue metadata and preview unsupported second-VTT fields.','No bundled protected media, stable IDs, no account impersonation, and explicit unsupported mappings.','P1','open','runtime','SRC-AUDIO-CORRECTION-142'),
('O-301','research','Test the private-audio demo against a generic jukebox message','A dramatic demo may win attention while still failing to communicate a payment-worthy job.','A/B test â€œthe rogue hears the whisperâ€ against a general immersive-audio/jukebox message with qualified buyers.','Recipient/scene message wins attention, non-zero price choice, and pilot commitment.','P2','open','product-research','SRC-SELECTIVE-AUDIO-141'),
('O-302','research','Measure whether Audio Secrets is broad or professional-only','Professional and horror GMs may pay while ordinary tables use voice chat or macros.','Compare price, repeat-use intent, saved prep, exact-alternative rejection, and pilot commitment across home, paid, organized-play, and narrative cohorts.','Cohort-specific WTP, rejection reasons, and a documented market-size decision.','P1','open','product-research','SRC-AUDIO-CORRECTION-142');

INSERT OR REPLACE INTO kb_trials(trial_id,area,symptom,attempted_approach,failure_cause,correction,evidence_status,source_id) VALUES
('T-141','market-selection','A fresh community scan found a vivid private/subset audio request with a direct eye-catching demo.','Build another jukebox or assume audio-module payment transfers to a new utility.','Foundry playlists are global, but recipient-aware APIs and existing modules/macros already cover pieces; no product-specific WTP yet.','Open Audio Secrets only as a recipient/scene/queue buyer gate with exact-alternative, price, pilot, rights, and portability checks.','Fresh conditional lead recorded; no product selected.','SRC-SELECTIVE-AUDIO-141'),
('T-142','market-selection','The premium audio audit confirmed category spending but weakened the new-product claim.','Treat Patreon audio, Narrator''s Jukebox, Playlist Plus, or a polished demo as proof that routing will sell.','Payments may be for music content, curation, polish, or maintenance; home-table substitutes remain strong.','Separate audio-heavy professional cohorts from home controls and require one-time routing WTP plus two pilots; continue the wide search if niche-only.','Direct-incumbent/payer correction recorded; no product selected.','SRC-AUDIO-CORRECTION-142');

INSERT OR REPLACE INTO kb_metadata(key,value) VALUES
('research_status_current','#1-#144 complete as research passes; generic Audio Secrets utility demoted after cross-VTT/current-package correction; Whisper Drop-In is the strongest new conditional product hypothesis because premium original content supplies a clearer payment path and private audio supplies the demo; Attendance-Resilient Side Session remains the first bounded payer gate; Dungeon Master''s Forge remains backburnered; no product selected');

INSERT OR REPLACE INTO kb_sources(source_id,title,source_kind,scope,authority,status,location,captured_at,version_fingerprint,notes) VALUES
('SRC-AUDIO-PORTABILITY-143','Selective audio cross-VTT portability correction','project','project','Current Soundscape Adventure, Roll20 Jukebox/Jukebox Plus, official Roll20 player roles, and Owlbear extension documentation','active','..\\PRODUCT_RESEARCH.md','2026-09-26','143 audio-routing/current-package/cross-vtt correction pass','Generic Audio Secrets utility demoted; neutral route manifest retained as reusable asset'),
('SRC-WHISPER-DROPIN-144','Whisper Drop-In productized content wrapper','project','project','Foundry premium-content and publisher guidance, current Soundscape Adventure, Whisper As, Louder Whispers, Drop-in Dungeons, Oronder, and original-content hypothesis','active','..\\PRODUCT_RESEARCH.md','2026-09-26','144 premium-content/asymmetric-clue/payer/rights/portability pass','Strongest new conditional hypothesis; no product selected and Dungeon Master''s Forge remains backburnered');

INSERT OR REPLACE INTO kb_facts(fact_id,domain,subject_no,title,statement,scope,evidence_class,status,source_id,tags) VALUES
('F-621','competition','', 'Current Foundry audio packages occupy generic soundscape automation','Soundscape Adventure is current through Foundry 14 and provides a cross-world sound library, moods, random/sequential loops, intensity, and triggers from regions, combats, and scenes.','project','static','provisional','SRC-AUDIO-PORTABILITY-143','competition,soundscape-adventure,foundry,audio,moods,triggers'),
('F-622','competition','', 'Roll20 already occupies the generic playlist control surface','Roll20 provides a global Jukebox and its Jukebox Plus documentation covers playlists, albums, looping, previews, styled feedback, and backup handouts.','project','static','provisional','SRC-AUDIO-PORTABILITY-143','competition,roll20,jukebox,jukebox-plus,playlist,backup'),
('F-623','portability','', 'Owlbear portability is an extension package, not runtime parity','Owlbear Rodeo supports manifest-loaded extensions, popovers, tools, and custom context menus, but a portable audio product would need its own extension and cannot assume a shared audio engine.','project','static','provisional','SRC-AUDIO-PORTABILITY-143','portability,owlbear,extensions,manifest,popover,unsupported'),
('F-624','portability-rights','', 'The portable audio boundary is intent metadata only','A neutral route manifest can preserve user-owned asset references, recipient scope, trigger, queue, duration, reward/clue linkage, and unsupported fields; it cannot guarantee equivalent playback, hosting, auth, or permission semantics.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-AUDIO-PORTABILITY-143','portability,manifest,route,rights,unsupported,second-vtt'),
('F-625','market-selection','', 'Generic Audio Secrets is too crowded for first implementation','Foundry Soundscape Adventure, Roll20 Jukebox/Jukebox Plus, recipient macros, Token Audio FX, Whisper As, and Owlbear extensions make a broad cross-VTT audio utility expensive to differentiate and maintain.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-AUDIO-PORTABILITY-143','market-selection,audio-secrets,crowded,demotion,no-product-selected'),
('F-626','market','', 'Premium content provides a direct payment path','Foundry''s premium-content and publisher guidance explicitly supports paid assets, adventures, audio packs, content keys, Patreon access, and one-time or recurring publisher delivery.','project','static','provisional','SRC-WHISPER-DROPIN-144','market,premium-content,audio,adventure,payment,foundry'),
('F-627','competition','', 'Existing modules cover private delivery components','Whisper As supports selected recipients and in-character aliases; Louder Whispers makes private messages noticeable; Soundscape Adventure covers ambient organization and triggers.','project','static','provisional','SRC-WHISPER-DROPIN-144','competition,whisper-as,louder-whispers,soundscape,private,clues'),
('F-628','market-product-boundary','', 'Whisper Drop-In combines original content with asymmetric delivery','The provisional product is a 60â€“120 minute, no-canon variable-party scenario with private audio clues, clean resolution, explicit reward/clue export, player-safe recap, and no hidden writes to the main campaign.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-WHISPER-DROPIN-144','product-boundary,whisper-drop-in,content,audio,variable-party,recap'),
('F-629','buyer-pain','', 'Whisper Drop-In has a clearer payer than a generic audio utility','Paid/professional GMs, organized-play and rotating-party hosts, and horror/investigation GMs can value a ready-to-run fallback and an immediately visible asymmetric clue mechanic; home groups remain a negative control.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-WHISPER-DROPIN-144','buyer-pain,paid-gm,organized-play,horror,investigation,negative-control'),
('F-630','market-selection','', 'Whisper Drop-In is the strongest new hypothesis but remains unvalidated','Advance only if qualified buyers prefer it over cancellation, free PDF, premium adventure, Drop-in Dungeons, Oronder, Soundscape plus Whisper As, generic audio packs, and manual play; choose a non-zero price and complete pilots with rights/runtime/portability proof.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-WHISPER-DROPIN-144','market-selection,whisper-drop-in,price,pilot,rights,portability,no-product-selected');

INSERT OR REPLACE INTO kb_decisions(decision_id,topic,decision,rationale,scope,status,owner,source_id,next_review) VALUES
('D-263','market-selection','Demote generic Audio Secrets as a first product after the cross-VTT/current-package correction.','Soundscape Adventure, Roll20 Jukebox/Jukebox Plus, recipient helpers, and Owlbear extensions occupy or fragment the utility surface.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-AUDIO-PORTABILITY-143',NULL),
('D-264','portability-rights','Retain only a neutral audio-route manifest as a reusable asset.','Intent metadata is portable, but playback, account, hosting, and permission semantics are VTT-specific.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-AUDIO-PORTABILITY-143',NULL),
('D-265','market-selection','Open Whisper Drop-In as the strongest new conditional product hypothesis.','A complete paid scenario has a clearer payment path than a utility, while asymmetric private clues provide an eye-catching differentiator.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-WHISPER-DROPIN-144',NULL),
('D-266','market-product-boundary','Keep Whisper Drop-In original/content-first and Foundry-first.','The offer must be a ready-to-run experience, not a new audio manager or copied D&D rules/content; second-VTT packaging begins with PDF/audio/manifest.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-WHISPER-DROPIN-144',NULL),
('D-267','market-selection','Run a separate Whisper Drop-In buyer gate at $15/$25/$39/no purchase.','Premium content supplies category payment evidence, but the buyer must prefer this exact scenario and explain whether the value is content, asymmetric delivery, or both.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-WHISPER-DROPIN-144',NULL),
('D-268','market-selection','Continue the ordinary-table search if Whisper Drop-In pays only as professional content.','A viable paid-GM niche is not enough to satisfy the broad ordinary-table objective without cohort evidence.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-WHISPER-DROPIN-144',NULL);

INSERT OR REPLACE INTO kb_open_items(item_id,item_class,title,problem,next_action,evidence_needed,priority,status,owner,source_id) VALUES
('O-303','research','Run the Whisper Drop-In buyer-choice and price gate','A premium one-shot, free PDF, or current side-session workflow may be sufficient and the audio mechanism may not affect purchase.','Recruit paid/professional, organized-play, horror/investigation, and home-control cohorts; show the exact scenario and alternatives at $15/$25/$39/no purchase.','5/8 qualified preference, 3/8 non-zero choices, two pilots, and separate content-versus-delivery reasons.','P0','open','product-research','SRC-WHISPER-DROPIN-144'),
('O-304','research','Test Whisper Drop-In content quality and repeat-use value','A clever mechanism cannot rescue weak pacing, unclear clues, poor replayability, or excessive GM setup.','Run a scripted 60â€“120 minute pilot with missing-player/variable-party variants and record prep time, clue comprehension, resolution quality, and re-use intent.','Two real pilots, low prep, clear asymmetric clue delivery, clean exit, and retention/recommendation evidence.','P0','open','product-research','SRC-WHISPER-DROPIN-144'),
('O-305','research','Compare Whisper Drop-In with exact paid and free alternatives','Buyers may choose a free PDF, another premium adventure, Drop-in Dungeons, Oronder, a duplicate world, or cancellation.','Run the same attendance/side-session incident through each alternative and code the reason for choosing or rejecting Whisper Drop-In.','Named residual failure and explicit preference over each alternative.','P0','open','product-research','SRC-WHISPER-DROPIN-144'),
('O-306','implementation','Prove original-content and audio licensing boundaries','Adventure text, stat blocks, art, voice, music, and sound effects can create rights obligations.','Use original story, original or licensed audio/art, SRD/permitted rules references, attribution records, and no copied publisher text.','Rights checklist, asset provenance, redistribution terms, and a deletable user-owned-media boundary.','P0','open','runtime','SRC-WHISPER-DROPIN-144'),
('O-307','implementation','Build the two-client Whisper Drop-In Foundry fixture only after buyer proof','Late join, missing players, private clues, reconnect, duplicate delivery, and reward export can break the experience or leak hidden state.','Use synthetic actors and original audio to test recipient state, clue idempotence, safe recap, explicit reward export, reconnect, and main-campaign isolation.','No secret leak, no duplicate clue, deterministic reconnect, safe exit, no unintended main-world writes.','P0','open','runtime','SRC-WHISPER-DROPIN-144'),
('O-308','research','Test Whisper Drop-In packaging on a second VTT','Roll20 and Owlbear support different audio, extension, and content-delivery models.','Package original PDF/audio/manifest for Roll20 and Owlbear as a read-only/manual import before attempting a runtime adapter.','One second-VTT package, unsupported fields documented, no parity claim, and no account impersonation.','P1','open','runtime','SRC-AUDIO-PORTABILITY-143');

INSERT OR REPLACE INTO kb_trials(trial_id,area,symptom,attempted_approach,failure_cause,correction,evidence_status,source_id) VALUES
('T-143','market-selection','The cross-VTT audit found generic selective audio crowded and technically fragmented.','Treat a neutral audio route manifest as proof that the same audio utility can be sold across Foundry, Roll20, and Owlbear.','Foundry, Roll20, and Owlbear expose different audio and extension semantics; current packages already occupy generic control.','Demote Audio Secrets utility and retain only intent metadata; test a content-first wrapper instead.','Cross-VTT/current-package correction recorded; no product selected.','SRC-AUDIO-PORTABILITY-143'),
('T-144','market-selection','A content-first asymmetric-audio scenario has a clearer payment path than an audio utility.','Bundle private audio into an original ready-to-run side-session and assume premium-content payment transfers.','Premium content establishes payment category, but exact content quality, alternatives, rights, professional-only breadth, and portability remain unproven.','Open Whisper Drop-In as a separate buyer gate with exact alternatives, one-time pricing, two pilots, rights proof, and second-VTT packaging.','Strongest new conditional hypothesis recorded; no product selected.','SRC-WHISPER-DROPIN-144');

INSERT OR REPLACE INTO kb_metadata(key,value) VALUES
('research_status_current','#1-#147 complete as research passes; generic Audio Secrets utility demoted after cross-VTT/current-package correction; Whisper Drop-In remains the strongest new conditional content hypothesis; Accessible Table Kit is the strongest fresh underserved-need hypothesis but is specialist and unvalidated; resource/timer utility rejected after incumbent correction; Attendance-Resilient Side Session remains the first bounded payer gate; Dungeon Master''s Forge remains backburnered; no product selected');

INSERT OR REPLACE INTO kb_sources(source_id,title,source_kind,scope,authority,status,location,captured_at,version_fingerprint,notes) VALUES
('SRC-RESOURCE-CORRECTION-145','Expedition and resource pressure correction','project','project','Community world-clock and torch requests, current Expedition Tracker, Light Sources, Party Operations, SessionFlow, and Flip Timer','active','..\\PRODUCT_RESEARCH.md','2026-09-26','145 resource/time/torch incumbent correction pass','Generic Resource Steward rejected; neutral resource-event and countdown contracts retained'),
('SRC-ACCESSIBLE-TABLE-146','Accessible Table Kit fresh lead','project','project','Community accessibility reports, Foundry Navigator, Accessibility Enhancements, player orientation, and current character-builder alternatives','active','..\\PRODUCT_RESEARCH.md','2026-09-26','146 accessibility/player-experience/payer pass','Conditional specialist lead; no product selected'),
('SRC-ACCESSIBLE-TABLE-CORRECTION-147','Accessible Table Kit market and portability correction','project','project','Current Foundry package catalog, Foundry module-management guidance, Foundry Navigator, Accessibility Enhancements, and Owlbear extension verification','active','..\\PRODUCT_RESEARCH.md','2026-09-26','147 accessibility/support-matrix/cross-vtt correction pass','Requires qualified incident, non-zero price, pilots, and read-only second-VTT contract');

INSERT OR REPLACE INTO kb_facts(fact_id,domain,subject_no,title,statement,scope,evidence_class,status,source_id,tags) VALUES
('F-631','buyer-pain','', 'World-clock resource reminders are a repeated community request','A community request asks for timers keyed to in-game world time for wandering-monster checks and torch burn-out rather than real seconds.','project','static','provisional','SRC-RESOURCE-CORRECTION-145','buyer-pain,world-clock,timer,torch,community'),
('F-632','buyer-pain','', 'System-agnostic torch burn-down is an explicit request','A separate request asks for a Shadowdark-style torch timer that consumes inventory, shows time remaining, and can announce a flavorful burn-out message for 5e or other systems.','project','static','provisional','SRC-RESOURCE-CORRECTION-145','buyer-pain,torch,system-agnostic,resource,community'),
('F-633','competition','', 'Expedition Tracker occupies basic expedition turns and timed effects','Expedition Tracker supports dungeon and overland turns, optional wandering-monster rolls, and timed effects that can apply and remove light sources.','project','static','provisional','SRC-RESOURCE-CORRECTION-145','competition,expedition-tracker,turns,wanderers,timed-effects'),
('F-634','competition','', 'Light Sources occupies inventory-backed torch burn-down','Light Sources is current through Foundry 14 and provides one-click inventory-backed lighting, in-game or real-time durations, automatic burn-out, chat notices, and multiple light patterns.','project','static','provisional','SRC-RESOURCE-CORRECTION-145','competition,light-sources,torch,inventory,burn-down,foundry14'),
('F-635','competition','', 'Campaign pressure and timer packages close the broad resource surface','Party Operations covers watches, marching order, torchlight, supplies, readiness, and campaign pressure; SessionFlow covers travel watches, supply/fatigue, progress clocks, and broadcast state; Flip Timer covers shared countdowns.','project','static','provisional','SRC-RESOURCE-CORRECTION-145','competition,party-operations,sessionflow,flip-timer,resources,pressure'),
('F-636','market-selection','', 'Resource interest is not new-product WTP','Community requests and category coverage establish a real problem but do not show that buyers will pay for another generic timer, resource ledger, or expedition dashboard.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-RESOURCE-CORRECTION-145','market-selection,resource,timer,wtp,rejected'),
('F-637','buyer-pain','', 'Accessibility failure is a recurring Foundry concern','A feature discussion reports poor screen-reader and keyboard-only accessibility, and community reports describe difficulty making Foundry text and controls usable for vision-impaired players.','project','static','provisional','SRC-ACCESSIBLE-TABLE-146','buyer-pain,accessibility,screen-reader,keyboard,vision'),
('F-638','competition','', 'Foundry Navigator is a current D&D5e accessibility incumbent','Foundry Navigator supports Foundry v13/v14 D&D5e keyboard-first and screen-reader workflows across sheets, combat, token movement, announcements, low resolution, and focus recovery, while acknowledging incomplete support.','project','static','provisional','SRC-ACCESSIBLE-TABLE-146','competition,foundry-navigator,dnd5e,screen-reader,keyboard,focus'),
('F-639','competition','', 'Accessibility Enhancements is an older PF2e-oriented incumbent','Accessibility Enhancements provides drag-and-drop alternatives, audio feedback, and high-contrast PF2e sheets, but its latest verified version is through Foundry 12.','project','static','provisional','SRC-ACCESSIBLE-TABLE-146','competition,accessibility-enhancements,pf2e,high-contrast,foundry12'),
('F-640','market-product-boundary','', 'Accessible Table Kit must remain a player-local accessibility layer','The candidate should provide semantic navigation, announcements, focus recovery, low-resolution layout, token/scene lists, and native-sheet escape hatches without copying rules or becoming a new automation engine.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-ACCESSIBLE-TABLE-146','product-boundary,accessibility,player-local,keyboard,screen-reader,no-rules-engine'),
('F-641','buyer','', 'Accessibility has a qualified payer segment but is not broad by default','Likely payers are GMs with a named disabled player, paid GMs, schools/libraries, organized-play hosts, and accessibility-conscious communities; ordinary home tables with no incident are a negative control.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-ACCESSIBLE-TABLE-146','buyer,paid-gm,school,organized-play,accessibility,negative-control'),
('F-642','portability','', 'Accessibility portability is semantic-contract portability','Keyboard commands, announcements, focus targets, preferences, and unsupported controls can be described neutrally, but Foundry, Roll20, and Owlbear do not share a common accessibility runtime.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-ACCESSIBLE-TABLE-CORRECTION-147','portability,accessibility,semantic-contract,roll20,owlbear,unsupported'),
('F-643','market','', 'Accessibility support carries a large maintenance matrix','A commercial accessibility layer would need a bounded supported matrix across system sheets, browsers, screen readers, third-party modules, and changing Foundry markup; every unsupported path can become a support incident.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-ACCESSIBLE-TABLE-CORRECTION-147','market,support,maintenance,screen-reader,third-party,foundry'),
('F-644','market-selection','', 'Accessible Table Kit requires specialist buyer validation','The product must beat Foundry Navigator, Accessibility Enhancements, native OS tools, custom CSS, and the exact system sheet on a named failure before a price claim is credible.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-ACCESSIBLE-TABLE-CORRECTION-147','market-selection,accessibility,exact-alternatives,price,validation'),
('F-645','market-selection','', 'Accessible Table Kit is the strongest fresh need but remains unselected','Accessibility has clearer human need and less generic saturation than resource timers, but it is not selected until qualified buyers choose a non-zero price, complete pilots, and accept the bounded scope.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-ACCESSIBLE-TABLE-CORRECTION-147','market-selection,accessibility,conditional,no-product-selected'),
('F-646','scope','', 'Dungeon Master''s Forge remains backburnered','The fresh research must not reopen or modify Dungeon Master''s Forge; its assets may be reconsidered only after a separate product passes the market gates.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-ACCESSIBLE-TABLE-CORRECTION-147','scope,dungeon-masters-forge,backburner,no-edit');

INSERT OR REPLACE INTO kb_decisions(decision_id,topic,decision,rationale,scope,status,owner,source_id,next_review) VALUES
('D-269','market-selection','Reject a generic Resource Steward, torch timer, or expedition dashboard as the next product.','Expedition Tracker, Light Sources, Party Operations, SessionFlow, and Flip Timer occupy the broad surface and community interest does not prove WTP.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-RESOURCE-CORRECTION-145',NULL),
('D-270','portability-rights','Retain only neutral resource-event and countdown contracts from the resource scan.','Event and countdown intent can be reused, but system inventory, world time, light, and mutation semantics are not portable by default.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-RESOURCE-CORRECTION-145',NULL),
('D-271','market-selection','Open Accessible Table Kit only as a conditional specialist buyer gate.','The accessibility need is concrete and less crowded than generic QoL, but current Foundry Navigator and community tools cover important slices.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-ACCESSIBLE-TABLE-146',NULL),
('D-272','market-product-boundary','Keep Accessible Table Kit player-local, semantic, and non-rules-authoritative.','A new rules engine or copied system content would increase correctness, licensing, and support risk; the value is access to already-authorized table actions.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-ACCESSIBLE-TABLE-146',NULL),
('D-273','buyer-segmentation','Test accessibility buyers separately from ordinary home tables.','GMs with a named disability/access failure, paid tables, schools, and organizers may pay while ordinary tables may not; broad WTP cannot be inferred.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-ACCESSIBLE-TABLE-146',NULL),
('D-274','portability-rights','Use a semantic accessibility contract for second-VTT work.','Commands, announcements, focus targets, preferences, and unsupported controls can travel, but separate clients and user tests are required for runtime behavior.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-ACCESSIBLE-TABLE-CORRECTION-147',NULL),
('D-275','market-selection','Run the Accessible Table Kit gate at $15/$30/$60/no purchase.','The price must follow a named failure and exact-alternative comparison; sponsorship, gratitude, or general social value is not product WTP.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-ACCESSIBLE-TABLE-CORRECTION-147',NULL),
('D-276','market-selection','Continue the broad search if accessibility payment is specialist-only or support-based.','A high-impact niche may be worthwhile but does not satisfy the broad ordinary-table objective without broader evidence.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-ACCESSIBLE-TABLE-CORRECTION-147',NULL),
('D-277','scope','Keep Dungeon Master''s Forge backburnered and untouched during the fresh search.','The user explicitly requested a new product search; DMF assets remain reusable background material only.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-ACCESSIBLE-TABLE-CORRECTION-147',NULL);

INSERT OR REPLACE INTO kb_open_items(item_id,item_class,title,problem,next_action,evidence_needed,priority,status,owner,source_id) VALUES
('O-309','research','Verify whether any qualified buyer has a resource failure that survives current modules','Generic torch and expedition requests may be satisfied by current packages or hand-waving.','Recruit survival, expedition, and paid GMs with a named failure and compare the exact incumbent stack before reopening Resource Steward.','Named repeated failure, exact-alternative rejection, non-zero price, and two pilots.','P1','open','product-research','SRC-RESOURCE-CORRECTION-145'),
('O-310','research','Compare resource/timer workflows against current packages','A prettier timer can duplicate Light Sources, Expedition Tracker, Party Operations, SessionFlow, or Flip Timer.','Run matched consume, recover, threshold, world-time, real-time, pause, and announcement tasks.','Reason-coded rejection of each exact alternative and no silent rule writes.','P1','open','product-research','SRC-RESOURCE-CORRECTION-145'),
('O-311','implementation','Preserve a neutral resource-event and countdown contract','Inventory, light, world time, and actor updates are system-specific.','Record resource identity, event, duration, policy, provenance, unsupported state, and receipt without mutating a live world.','Read-only mapping works on two fixtures and preserves unsupported semantics.','P2','open','runtime','SRC-RESOURCE-CORRECTION-145'),
('O-312','research','Recruit qualified accessibility tables for Accessible Table Kit','Accessibility agreement alone does not establish a buyer or define the supported workflow.','Recruit tables with a named screen-reader, keyboard-only, low-vision, motor, or low-resolution incident.','8 qualified participants with exact failure, current workaround, and payer identity.','P0','open','product-research','SRC-ACCESSIBLE-TABLE-146'),
('O-313','research','Compare Accessible Table Kit against exact accessibility alternatives','Foundry Navigator, Accessibility Enhancements, native OS tools, custom CSS, and system sheets may solve the named failure.','Run the same join, chat, sheet, token, turn, and focus-recovery task through each control.','5/8 preference over exact alternatives and coded rejection reasons.','P0','open','product-research','SRC-ACCESSIBLE-TABLE-CORRECTION-147'),
('O-314','implementation','Build a synthetic accessibility fixture before implementation','Screen-reader and keyboard behavior can fail silently across sheets and third-party modules.','Use supported synthetic D&D5e and PF2e sheets, keyboard-only input, screen-reader announcements, focus transitions, and low resolution.','No inaccessible critical control, lost focus, wrong-user disclosure, or unauthorized action on supported scope.','P0','open','runtime','SRC-ACCESSIBLE-TABLE-146'),
('O-315','research','Test Accessible Table Kit price and payer identity','A GM may value inclusion but not pay personally, while a school or paid GM may sponsor the tool.','Ask $15/$30/$60/no purchase and record player, GM, organizer, school, and sponsorship reasons separately.','3/8 qualified non-zero choices and a clear payer role.','P0','open','product-research','SRC-ACCESSIBLE-TABLE-CORRECTION-147'),
('O-316','research','Test accessibility retention across three sessions','A one-time rescue may not support a durable product or update burden.','Run three sessions with the same supported player and record recurring use, setup, regressions, and renewal/update rationale.','Two pilots complete three sessions and retain or repurchase the bounded tool.','P1','open','product-research','SRC-ACCESSIBLE-TABLE-CORRECTION-147'),
('O-317','implementation','Define privacy and permission boundaries for accessibility state','Player preferences, spoken text, hidden information, and personal accessibility needs can be sensitive.','Keep preference state player-local where possible, minimize logs, and use existing permissions for all table actions.','No medical inference, raw sensitive-data leak, hidden-content announcement, or unauthorized action.','P0','open','runtime','SRC-ACCESSIBLE-TABLE-CORRECTION-147'),
('O-318','implementation','Audit browser, screen-reader, system-sheet, and module support costs','Broad accessibility claims can create an unbounded maintenance and support obligation.','Publish a versioned support matrix and an explicit unsupported-control escape to native Foundry.','Bounded supported matrix, reproducible issue reports, and no implied universal WCAG/runtime claim.','P0','open','runtime','SRC-ACCESSIBLE-TABLE-CORRECTION-147'),
('O-319','implementation','Map the semantic accessibility contract to one second VTT','Foundry UI hooks do not imply Roll20 or Owlbear behavior.','Map preferences, commands, announcements, focus targets, and unsupported actions to a read-only second-VTT receipt.','One second-VTT artifact with unsupported states and no runtime-parity claim.','P2','open','runtime','SRC-ACCESSIBLE-TABLE-CORRECTION-147'),
('O-320','research','Continue the wide search if accessibility is high-impact but noncommercial','A specialist need can be valuable without being the broad market product requested.','Do not promote from social importance or community gratitude; search the next payer problem if the gate fails.','Evidence-weighted decision and a fresh candidate or explicit negative control.','P1','open','product-research','SRC-ACCESSIBLE-TABLE-CORRECTION-147'),
('O-321','research','Keep Dungeon Master''s Forge out of the active product comparison','The user asked for a fresh product and DMF is backburnered.','Do not edit or reopen DMF; reuse assets only after a separate product passes market gates.','No DMF implementation changes and explicit backburner status in the ledger.','P1','open','product-research','SRC-ACCESSIBLE-TABLE-CORRECTION-147');

INSERT OR REPLACE INTO kb_trials(trial_id,area,symptom,attempted_approach,failure_cause,correction,evidence_status,source_id) VALUES
('T-145','market-selection','Fresh scan found explicit requests for world-clock timers, system-agnostic torch burn-down, and resource pressure.','Open a new generic timer, torch, or expedition dashboard.','Expedition Tracker, Light Sources, Party Operations, SessionFlow, and Flip Timer occupy the broad behavior; WTP is absent.','Reject the generic utility and retain only neutral resource/countdown contracts.','Current-incumbent correction recorded; no product selected.','SRC-RESOURCE-CORRECTION-145'),
('T-146','market-selection','Fresh accessibility scan found recurring screen-reader, keyboard-only, and low-vision pain.','Assume an accessibility need is automatically a broad paid product.','Foundry Navigator, Accessibility Enhancements, native tools, and system-specific workflows cover important slices; payer segment is uncertain.','Open Accessible Table Kit only as a qualified-incident buyer gate with bounded scope.','Conditional specialist lead recorded; no product selected.','SRC-ACCESSIBLE-TABLE-146'),
('T-147','market-selection','Accessibility portability and support burden are larger than the initial gap suggested.','Promise a universal cross-VTT accessibility layer.','Foundry, Roll20, and Owlbear have different client/extension runtimes; browser, screen-reader, sheet, and module support can be unbounded.','Require exact-alternative preference, non-zero price, two pilots, a support matrix, privacy proof, and a read-only second-VTT contract.','Market/portability correction recorded; no product selected.','SRC-ACCESSIBLE-TABLE-CORRECTION-147');

INSERT OR REPLACE INTO kb_metadata(key,value) VALUES
('research_status_current','#1-#150 complete as research passes; generic Audio Secrets utility demoted after cross-VTT/current-package correction; Whisper Drop-In remains the strongest new conditional content hypothesis; Accessible Table Kit remains a specialist accessibility hypothesis; broad cognitive/player-focus utility rejected; Migration Safe Harbor / VTT BridgeCheck is the strongest fresh high-urgency GM hypothesis but remains episodic and unvalidated; resource/timer utility rejected; Attendance-Resilient Side Session remains the first bounded payer gate; Dungeon Master''s Forge remains backburnered; no product selected');

INSERT OR REPLACE INTO kb_sources(source_id,title,source_kind,scope,authority,status,location,captured_at,version_fingerprint,notes) VALUES
('SRC-COGNITIVE-LOAD-CORRECTION-148','Cognitive load and player-focus correction','project','project','Current PF2e player pain, Player Pilot, Foundry Navigator, Stylish Action HUD, Carolingian UI, and SessionFlow','active','..\\PRODUCT_RESEARCH.md','2026-09-26','148 cognitive/player-focus/incumbent correction pass','Broad simpler-Foundry product rejected; accessibility remains incident-gated'),
('SRC-MIGRATION-SAFE-HARBOR-149','Migration Safe Harbor fresh GM-payer lead','project','project','Current DDB-Importer, community import/migration failures, Adventure Importer/Exporter, PDF-to-Foundry, and migration discussions','active','..\\PRODUCT_RESEARCH.md','2026-09-26','149 post-import-assurance/migration/payer pass','Narrow VTT BridgeCheck successor; no product selected'),
('SRC-MIGRATION-SAFE-HARBOR-CORRECTION-150','Migration Safe Harbor direct-incumbent and rights correction','project','project','Foundry Adventure Documents, Scene Packer, Asset Auditor, Lore Reference Board, RPGNautas File Manager, DDB-Importer, and migration rights discussion','active','..\\PRODUCT_RESEARCH.md','2026-09-26','150 import-repair/rights/portability correction pass','Episodic buyer gate only; no converter, scraping, or credential proxy');

INSERT OR REPLACE INTO kb_facts(fact_id,domain,subject_no,title,statement,scope,evidence_class,status,source_id,tags) VALUES
('F-647','buyer-pain','', 'General Foundry cognitive-load pain is real but heterogeneous','A current PF2e discussion reports players repeatedly losing time in a complex character sheet with too many tabs, while other users describe tab management, HUDs, and system learning as sufficient remedies.','project','static','provisional','SRC-COGNITIVE-LOAD-CORRECTION-148','buyer-pain,cognitive-load,pf2e,player,ui'),
('F-648','competition','', 'Player Pilot occupies simplified player control','Player Pilot provides a mobile-first player control panel for common actor actions, spells, features, movement, targeting, pings, rests, and requests without requiring the full character sheet.','project','static','provisional','SRC-COGNITIVE-LOAD-CORRECTION-148','competition,player-pilot,player-panel,mobile,actions'),
('F-649','competition','', 'HUD and UI-overhaul products occupy broad player simplification','Foundry Navigator, Stylish Action HUD, Carolingian UI, SessionFlow, and system-specific HUD/configuration workflows cover substantial keyboard, action, presentation, focus, and clutter-reduction needs.','project','static','provisional','SRC-COGNITIVE-LOAD-CORRECTION-148','competition,foundry-navigator,stylish-action-hud,carolingian,sessionflow'),
('F-650','market-selection','', 'Broad Cognitive Access is not a differentiated product','The broad promise of a simpler Foundry experience mixes onboarding, system complexity, accessibility, HUD preference, and personal configuration; current alternatives make a new paid utility difficult to distinguish.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-COGNITIVE-LOAD-CORRECTION-148','market-selection,cognitive-access,focus-mode,rejected'),
('F-651','portability','', 'Semantic focus and action contracts remain reusable','Focus targets, announcements, keyboard commands, and player-action intents can be retained as neutral assets even though each VTT and system implements them differently.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-COGNITIVE-LOAD-CORRECTION-148','portability,focus,announcements,player-actions,contract'),
('F-652','buyer-pain','', 'Post-import false-green failures are concrete','A community report describes scenes, journals, actors, and sounds importing while journal links remain unreferenced, including internal links, even in a blank test world.','project','static','provisional','SRC-MIGRATION-SAFE-HARBOR-149','buyer-pain,migration,broken-links,import,false-green'),
('F-653','portability-rights','', 'VTT migration has no common formal portability standard','A current migration discussion reports that D&D Beyond and Roll20 lack a formal common export/import path, Roll20 export is constrained, Foundry formats change, and converters are best effort.','project','static','provisional','SRC-MIGRATION-SAFE-HARBOR-149','portability,roll20,dndbeyond,foundry,migration,rights'),
('F-654','competition','', 'DDB-Importer already covers substantial D&D5e adventure import','Current DDB-Importer supports Foundry 14 and imports many D&D Beyond adventures with walls, lighting, journals, and monsters, alongside characters, items, encounters, maps, and other content.','project','static','provisional','SRC-MIGRATION-SAFE-HARBOR-149','competition,ddb-importer,dnd5e,adventures,foundry14'),
('F-655','market-product-boundary','', 'Migration Safe Harbor is a post-import assurance receipt','The candidate is a local, read-only, disposable-copy pass that checks links, assets, scene geometry, permissions, duplicates, overwrites, compatibility, unsupported fields, and play-tonight smoke conditions.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-MIGRATION-SAFE-HARBOR-149','product-boundary,migration,receipt,read-only,disposable-copy'),
('F-656','buyer','', 'Migration Safe Harbor has a clearer but episodic GM payer','Active migrating GMs, long-running campaign owners, paid GMs, and small publishers may pay to reduce migration deadline and game-night risk; ordinary players are not the payer.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-MIGRATION-SAFE-HARBOR-149','buyer,gm,paid-gm,migration,episodic,deadline'),
('F-657','competition','', 'Foundry-native packaging and repair tools close much of the assurance claim','Foundry Adventure Documents preserve internal links for Foundry imports; Scene Packer supplies an asset report; Asset Auditor finds missing paths; Lore Reference Board performs import-time link checks and relinking; RPGNautas advertises deep link repair.','project','static','provisional','SRC-MIGRATION-SAFE-HARBOR-CORRECTION-150','competition,adventure-documents,scene-packer,asset-auditor,lore-reference-board,link-repair'),
('F-658','market-selection','', 'The residual migration wedge is a named false-green, not migration in general','A new product must find a failure that remains after the exact source importer and current repair tools complete; otherwise manual cleanup or free modules rationally win.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-MIGRATION-SAFE-HARBOR-CORRECTION-150','market-selection,false-green,exact-alternatives,repair'),
('F-659','rights','', 'Migration Safe Harbor must not scrape or proxy source accounts','Roll20/D&D Beyond credentials, unsupported scraping, publisher-content retention, or license circumvention would create unacceptable platform and rights risk.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-MIGRATION-SAFE-HARBOR-CORRECTION-150','rights,credentials,scraping,roll20,dndbeyond,privacy'),
('F-660','portability','', 'The portable BridgeCheck artifact is a receipt, not a converter','A neutral receipt can contain IDs, document kinds, asset fingerprints, link states, package versions, permission scopes, check results, repair proposals, and unsupported states; runtime mutation remains VTT-specific.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-MIGRATION-SAFE-HARBOR-CORRECTION-150','portability,receipt,manifest,unsupported,second-vtt'),
('F-661','market-selection','', 'Migration Safe Harbor is stronger than resource or broad accessibility on payment intent','Migration deadlines and paid importers provide a clearer GM payment proxy than generic resource timers or general UI/accessibility interest, but this is category evidence and the use is episodic.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-MIGRATION-SAFE-HARBOR-CORRECTION-150','market-selection,payment-proxy,migration,episodic,comparison'),
('F-662','market-selection','', 'Migration Safe Harbor remains unselected','Promote only after qualified migrating GMs prefer the receipt over exact importer-plus-cleanup, choose a non-zero price, complete disposable-copy pilots, and accept the credential/content boundary.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-MIGRATION-SAFE-HARBOR-CORRECTION-150','market-selection,migration,price,pilot,no-product-selected');

INSERT OR REPLACE INTO kb_decisions(decision_id,topic,decision,rationale,scope,status,owner,source_id,next_review) VALUES
('D-278','market-selection','Reject a broad Cognitive Access, Focus Mode, or simpler-Foundry product.','Player Pilot, Foundry Navigator, HUDs, UI overhauls, SessionFlow, and system configuration occupy the broad cognitive-load surface.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-COGNITIVE-LOAD-CORRECTION-148',NULL),
('D-279','market-product-boundary','Keep Accessible Table Kit limited to named accessibility incidents.','General UI frustration mixes different problems and cannot transfer WTP to a screen-reader or keyboard product.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-COGNITIVE-LOAD-CORRECTION-148',NULL),
('D-280','portability-rights','Retain semantic focus, announcement, and player-action contracts as reusable assets.','Neutral intent is useful, but UI/runtime and system behavior are adapter-specific.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-COGNITIVE-LOAD-CORRECTION-148',NULL),
('D-281','market-selection','Reopen VTT BridgeCheck as Migration Safe Harbor, a post-import assurance gate.','Migration false-green incidents and deadlines create clearer GM value than another importer, but current importers and repair tools are strong controls.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-MIGRATION-SAFE-HARBOR-149',NULL),
('D-282','market-product-boundary','Keep Migration Safe Harbor read-only and disposable-copy based.','Live repair, account access, scraping, or content retention would create data-loss, credential, and rights risk.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-MIGRATION-SAFE-HARBOR-149',NULL),
('D-283','buyer-segmentation','Test active migrating and paid GMs separately from ordinary players.','Migration is a GM-owned, episodic risk; player interest cannot establish the payer or recurrence.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-MIGRATION-SAFE-HARBOR-149',NULL),
('D-284','market-selection','Compare Migration Safe Harbor against every exact importer and repair control before pricing.','DDB-Importer, R20 tools, PDF-to-Foundry, Adventure Documents, Scene Packer, Asset Auditor, Lore Reference Board, and RPGNautas already occupy major pieces.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-MIGRATION-SAFE-HARBOR-CORRECTION-150',NULL),
('D-285','market-selection','Run Migration Safe Harbor at $10/$25/$50/$75/no purchase as an episodic buyer gate.','The product must earn a one-time price from a named false-green failure; category importer payment is not enough.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-MIGRATION-SAFE-HARBOR-CORRECTION-150',NULL),
('D-286','portability-rights','Require a read-only receipt and clean credential/content boundary before any migration implementation.','The second VTT can consume evidence, but cross-account mutation, scraping, and license circumvention are out of scope.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-MIGRATION-SAFE-HARBOR-CORRECTION-150',NULL);

INSERT OR REPLACE INTO kb_open_items(item_id,item_class,title,problem,next_action,evidence_needed,priority,status,owner,source_id) VALUES
('O-322','research','Do not reopen broad Cognitive Access from general player frustration','PF2e sheet complexity and visual overload may be solved by system settings, Player Pilot, HUDs, or learning.','Require a named accessibility failure before using the Accessible Table Kit gate.','Exact incident, exact-alternative rejection, payer identity, and non-zero price.','P1','open','product-research','SRC-COGNITIVE-LOAD-CORRECTION-148'),
('O-323','implementation','Preserve semantic focus and action contracts','Foundry UI and system adapters should not be mistaken for portable runtime behavior.','Record focus target, announcement, keyboard command, action intent, permission scope, and unsupported state.','Two-client read-only mapping with no unauthorized action.','P2','open','runtime','SRC-COGNITIVE-LOAD-CORRECTION-148'),
('O-324','research','Recruit active migrating GMs with a named false-green failure','General portability frustration is not enough to pay for assurance.','Ask for source, importer, date, failed artifact, cleanup time, deadline, and current backup/clone workflow.','8 qualified GMs with a reproducible post-import incident or high-cost deadline.','P0','open','product-research','SRC-MIGRATION-SAFE-HARBOR-149'),
('O-325','research','Compare Migration Safe Harbor with the exact source importer','A receipt may add no value after DDB-Importer, R20Converter, PDF-to-Foundry, or the buyerâ€™s normal path.','Run matched synthetic/user-owned migrations through the exact importer and record unresolved work and time.','Named residual failure and reason-coded preference.','P0','open','product-research','SRC-MIGRATION-SAFE-HARBOR-CORRECTION-150'),
('O-326','research','Compare Migration Safe Harbor with current Foundry repair tools','Asset Auditor, Scene Packer, Lore Reference Board, RPGNautas, and native Adventure Documents cover large parts of the job.','Run the same broken-link, missing-asset, and import-repair fixture through each control.','5/8 qualified preference over exact controls before promotion.','P0','open','product-research','SRC-MIGRATION-SAFE-HARBOR-CORRECTION-150'),
('O-327','implementation','Build a disposable post-import assurance fixture','A live-world checker or repairer could damage campaign state or report false green.','Use synthetic/user-owned exports and clone worlds with links, assets, scenes, permissions, duplicates, version drift, and unsupported fields.','Live world unchanged, deterministic rerun, clear false/unknown/unsupported states, and rollback evidence.','P0','open','runtime','SRC-MIGRATION-SAFE-HARBOR-149'),
('O-328','implementation','Prove the credential and content rights boundary','Source accounts and publisher content may not be accessed, scraped, retained, or redistributed.','Inspect only user-owned post-import output; do not collect credentials or call source providers.','Written rights/credential matrix and a negative test proving no account/network dependency.','P0','open','runtime','SRC-MIGRATION-SAFE-HARBOR-CORRECTION-150'),
('O-329','research','Test Migration Safe Harbor price and payer role','Migration is episodic and the buyer may choose free cleanup or rebuild instead of a paid receipt.','Ask $10/$25/$50/$75/no purchase after the exact alternatives and code prevention, diagnosis, repair, and confidence value.','3/8 qualified non-zero choices and a clear GM/paid-GM/publisher payer.','P0','open','product-research','SRC-MIGRATION-SAFE-HARBOR-CORRECTION-150'),
('O-330','research','Test whether migration assurance earns repeat or durable one-time value','A single successful migration may not support updates or maintenance.','Run two migrations or an import plus a package update/restore scenario with the same buyer.','Two pilots and a defensible one-time purchase or repeat-use rationale.','P1','open','product-research','SRC-MIGRATION-SAFE-HARBOR-CORRECTION-150'),
('O-331','implementation','Define the versioned portable BridgeCheck receipt','A report that copies content or claims another VTT works identically would be unsafe and legally unclear.','Use IDs, kinds, fingerprints, package versions, link states, scopes, checks, repairs, and unsupported fields only.','Second-VTT read-only consumer accepts the receipt without account access or mutation.','P1','open','runtime','SRC-MIGRATION-SAFE-HARBOR-CORRECTION-150'),
('O-332','research','Test game-night confidence against a plain importer status','A dramatic receipt may be an attractive diagnostic without changing the buyerâ€™s decision.','A/B test â€œknow what broke before game nightâ€ against importer-complete, backup, and manual-check messages.','Receipt improves decision confidence, non-zero price choice, and pilot commitment.','P1','open','product-research','SRC-MIGRATION-SAFE-HARBOR-149'),
('O-333','research','Continue the broad search if Migration Safe Harbor only saves one migration','A high-cost one-time incident may be valuable but not the broad recurring product requested.','If the gate fails, search another payer problem rather than building a converter.','Evidence-weighted demotion and a new candidate or negative control.','P1','open','product-research','SRC-MIGRATION-SAFE-HARBOR-CORRECTION-150'),
('O-334','research','Keep Dungeon Master''s Forge out of Migration Safe Harbor work','The fresh candidate must not reopen DMF or merge its implementation scope.','Do not edit DMF; reuse only generic receipt/validation assets after the product gate.','No DMF changes and explicit backburner status.','P1','open','product-research','SRC-MIGRATION-SAFE-HARBOR-CORRECTION-150');

INSERT OR REPLACE INTO kb_trials(trial_id,area,symptom,attempted_approach,failure_cause,correction,evidence_status,source_id) VALUES
('T-148','market-selection','Broad player frustration was reframed as a universal cognitive-access or focus product.','Bundle simplified UI, onboarding, accessibility, HUD, and player actions into a new module.','Player Pilot, Foundry Navigator, HUDs, UI overhauls, SessionFlow, and system workflows already occupy the broad job.','Reject the broad product; keep accessibility incident-gated and retain only neutral semantic contracts.','Direct-incumbent correction recorded; no product selected.','SRC-COGNITIVE-LOAD-CORRECTION-148'),
('T-149','market-selection','Migration reports show imported worlds can be structurally present but not playable.','Build another converter or treat current importer completion as sufficient.','Broken links, missing assets, version drift, and unsupported provider portability create a residual post-import assurance problem.','Open Migration Safe Harbor as a read-only disposable-copy buyer gate.','Fresh high-urgency GM hypothesis recorded; no product selected.','SRC-MIGRATION-SAFE-HARBOR-149'),
('T-150','market-selection','Current Foundry repair/package tools occupy much of the migration assurance surface.','Assume migration pain or importer payment proves WTP for a new receipt.','Adventure Documents, Scene Packer, Asset Auditor, Lore Reference Board, RPGNautas, and DDB-Importer cover major paths; rights and recurrence remain weak.','Require named false-green failure, exact-alternative preference, non-zero price, two pilots, and clean second-VTT receipt before promotion.','Market/rights correction recorded; no product selected.','SRC-MIGRATION-SAFE-HARBOR-CORRECTION-150');

INSERT OR REPLACE INTO kb_metadata(key,value) VALUES
('research_status_current','#1-#163 complete as research passes; generic Audio Secrets utility demoted after cross-VTT/current-package correction; Whisper Drop-In remains a conditional content hypothesis; Accessible Table Kit remains a specialist accessibility hypothesis; broad cognitive/player-focus utility rejected; Migration Safe Harbor / VTT BridgeCheck remains a high-urgency but episodic migration hypothesis; paid-GM attendance economics confirmed but generic attendance software rejected; Table Rescue / Attendance-Resilient Side Session remains the first bounded payer gate; Session Continuity is a conditional reliability gate, not a selected product; rest/downtime broad automation demoted after current-module and portability correction; Playability Budget / Media Safe Pack is a conditional asset-heavy GM gate, not a selected product; Dungeon Master''s Forge remains backburnered; no product selected');

INSERT OR REPLACE INTO kb_sources(source_id,title,source_kind,scope,authority,status,location,captured_at,version_fingerprint,notes) VALUES
('SRC-MIGRATION-PAYMENT-151','Migration payment-proxy audit','project','project','Current DDB-Importer package/docs, Patreon access boundary, adventure docs, and migration discussions','active','..\\PRODUCT_RESEARCH.md','2026-09-26','151 importer-payment/maintenance/receipt-WTP correction pass','Importer payment strengthens payer recruitment but does not prove assurance-receipt WTP');

INSERT OR REPLACE INTO kb_facts(fact_id,domain,subject_no,title,statement,scope,evidence_class,status,source_id,tags) VALUES
('F-663','market','', 'DDB-Importer has a current paid-access and maintenance boundary','DDB-Importer is current through Foundry 14 and documents Patreon or user-run proxy access for some monster, adventure, sync, and support features, while maintaining multiple Foundry/D&D5e version lines.','project','static','provisional','SRC-MIGRATION-PAYMENT-151','market,ddb-importer,patreon,maintenance,foundry14'),
('F-664','buyer','', 'Active GMs pay for import capability when value is concrete','Current importer access and historical community discussions provide a category payment proxy for active GMs who value retained content, saved preparation, and ongoing compatibility.','project','static','provisional','SRC-MIGRATION-PAYMENT-151','buyer,gm,import,payment-proxy,prep,compatibility'),
('F-665','market-selection','', 'Importer payment does not prove receipt payment','An importer produces or transforms content, while Migration Safe Harbor only diagnoses uncertainty after import; category WTP cannot be transferred without a decision-changing false-green result.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-MIGRATION-PAYMENT-151','market-selection,wtp,receipt,importer,false-green,no-transfer'),
('F-666','buyer-pain','', 'Post-update regression checks may create repeat value','A buyer may have a second payment reason if a Foundry, system, or module update can silently invalidate a previously trusted imported campaign.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-MIGRATION-PAYMENT-151','buyer-pain,regression,update,version-drift,repeat-value'),
('F-667','competition','', 'Package warnings and manual clone tests are controls for regression assurance','Foundry package/version warnings, importer support paths, backups, and a manual disposable clone can detect or contain some post-update failures.','project','static','provisional','SRC-MIGRATION-PAYMENT-151','competition,package-warnings,backup,clone,regression'),
('F-668','rights','', 'Payment validation must exclude proxy and credential handling','Importer proxy access may require source-account credentials, but Migration Safe Harbor must inspect only user-owned output and must not collect cookies, operate a proxy, scrape, or retain publisher content.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-MIGRATION-PAYMENT-151','rights,credentials,proxy,scraping,publisher-content');

INSERT OR REPLACE INTO kb_decisions(decision_id,topic,decision,rationale,scope,status,owner,source_id,next_review) VALUES
('D-287','market-selection','Use importer payment only to recruit Migration Safe Harbor buyers, not to claim product WTP.','DDB-Importerâ€™s paid feature/support boundary shows a payer segment, while the receiptâ€™s value is a different job.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-MIGRATION-PAYMENT-151',NULL),
('D-288','market-selection','Add a post-update regression arm to the Migration Safe Harbor gate.','A one-time import may be too episodic; repeat value could come from checking an imported campaign after core/system/module updates.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-MIGRATION-PAYMENT-151',NULL),
('D-289','rights','Keep credentials, proxies, scraping, and source-content retention out of Migration Safe Harbor.','The assurance product must not reproduce the importerâ€™s account or licensing boundary.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-MIGRATION-PAYMENT-151',NULL);

INSERT OR REPLACE INTO kb_open_items(item_id,item_class,title,problem,next_action,evidence_needed,priority,status,owner,source_id) VALUES
('O-335','research','Separate importer payment from assurance payment','Paid importer access may value content transformation, not a receipt.','Recruit the same buyer for importer, exact cleanup, receipt-only, and post-update regression tasks.','Reason-coded payer choice and non-zero price for each job.','P0','open','product-research','SRC-MIGRATION-PAYMENT-151'),
('O-336','research','Test post-update regression value','Migration Safe Harbor may have no durable use after a successful import.','Re-run the disposable receipt after Foundry, D&D5e, and module updates; compare package warnings, importer support, backup, and manual clone.','Two pilots show a decision-changing result and a defensible one-time or repeat price.','P0','open','product-research','SRC-MIGRATION-PAYMENT-151'),
('O-337','implementation','Prove the receipt has no source-account dependency','A hidden proxy or credential path would turn assurance into an unsafe importer.','Run with synthetic/user-owned output and deny network/account access in the fixture.','No credential collection, source call, scraping, or publisher-content retention.','P0','open','runtime','SRC-MIGRATION-PAYMENT-151'),
('O-338','research','Continue the broad search if post-update assurance is still episodic','Importer/payment proxies may support a niche service without satisfying the broad market objective.','Keep Migration Safe Harbor conditional and open the next unrelated payer scan if repeat value fails.','Evidence-weighted demotion and a new candidate or negative control.','P1','open','product-research','SRC-MIGRATION-PAYMENT-151');

INSERT OR REPLACE INTO kb_trials(trial_id,area,symptom,attempted_approach,failure_cause,correction,evidence_status,source_id) VALUES
('T-151','market-selection','Importer access and maintenance have a real payment proxy.','Treat Patreon/importer payment as proof that buyers will pay for a post-import assurance receipt.','Importer transformation and maintenance value differ from diagnostic confidence; one-time migration may not recur.','Recruit importer payers, test receipt-only and post-update regression value separately, and keep the credential/content boundary clean.','Payment-proxy correction recorded; no product selected.','SRC-MIGRATION-PAYMENT-151');

INSERT OR REPLACE INTO kb_sources(source_id,title,source_kind,scope,authority,status,location,captured_at,version_fingerprint,notes) VALUES
('SRC-PAID-GM-ATTENDANCE-152','Paid-GM attendance economics','project','project','Current StartPlaying payment, refund, no-show, and GM-policy pages plus Warhorn event/payment surface','active','..\\PRODUCT_RESEARCH.md','2026-09-26','152 paid-GM/organized-play attendance economics pass','Attendance has money and seat consequences for qualified GMs, but platforms already own booking and payment policy'),
('SRC-ATTENDANCE-INCUMBENT-153','Attendance incumbent correction','project','project','StartPlaying, Warhorn, current SessionFlow, Scene Packer, and existing drop-in content','active','..\\PRODUCT_RESEARCH.md','2026-09-26','153 attendance/roster/session-tool correction pass','Reject generic attendance software; retain only content-shaped session rescue hypothesis'),
('SRC-SIDE-SESSION-GATE-154','Table Rescue product gate','project','project','Paid-GM policies, Foundry session tooling, premium drop-in alternatives, and portability boundary','active','..\\PRODUCT_RESEARCH.md','2026-09-26','154 table-rescue/variable-party/no-canon product gate','Conditional content candidate; no product selected');

INSERT OR REPLACE INTO kb_facts(fact_id,domain,subject_no,title,statement,scope,evidence_class,status,source_id,tags) VALUES
('F-669','buyer-pain','', 'Paid-session attendance has direct economic consequences','StartPlaying charges players per session, charges signed-up no-shows, and does not charge when the GM cancels; this makes seat utilization and session continuity a concrete paid-GM concern.','project','static','provisional','SRC-PAID-GM-ATTENDANCE-152','buyer-pain,paid-gm,attendance,no-show,seat-utilization'),
('F-670','competition','', 'Attendance policy is already owned by booking platforms','StartPlaying provides skip windows, charges, refunds, price waivers, player removal, and no-show guidance, while Warhorn provides event registration, schedules, table planning, and payments.','project','static','provisional','SRC-PAID-GM-ATTENDANCE-152','competition,startplaying,warhorn,refund,registration'),
('F-671','buyer-segmentation','', 'Qualified attendance buyers are paid and organized-play operators','Paid/professional GMs, organized-play hosts, and event organizers have revenue, seat, and reputation consequences that ordinary home tables often avoid by postponing.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-PAID-GM-ATTENDANCE-152','buyer,paid-gm,organized-play,event,negative-control'),
('F-672','market-selection','', 'Attendance pain does not justify a new roster module','The money signal validates a payer segment but not a new scheduler, roster, or cancellation tool because incumbents already perform those jobs.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-PAID-GM-ATTENDANCE-152','market-selection,attendance,roster,scheduler,incumbent'),
('F-673','buyer-pain','', 'The residual job is preserving value when party size changes','The unmet hypothesis is keeping a paid or high-value session worthwhile when one or more expected players disappear, not tracking attendance itself.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-PAID-GM-ATTENDANCE-152','buyer-pain,session-continuity,party-size,paid-gm'),
('F-674','competition','', 'SessionFlow occupies broad Foundry session orchestration','SessionFlow provides beat and scene sequencing, quick scenes, progress clocks, player widgets, recaps, and a player-facing canvas, weakening a generic session-dashboard pitch.','project','static','provisional','SRC-ATTENDANCE-INCUMBENT-153','competition,sessionflow,beats,scenes,player-panel'),
('F-675','competition','', 'Scene Packer and drop-in content lower emergency-prep cost','Scene Packer preserves links and assets across imported scenes, while existing drop-in products already sell minimal-preparation adventures.','project','static','provisional','SRC-ATTENDANCE-INCUMBENT-153','competition,scene-packer,drop-in,emergency-prep'),
('F-676','market-product-boundary','', 'Attendance Rescue must be content-shaped','A defensible wedge is a bounded no-canon side session with variable-party entry, an explicit exit, and campaign-safe reward or recap export rather than another attendance control panel.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-ATTENDANCE-INCUMBENT-153','product-boundary,no-canon,variable-party,reward-export'),
('F-677','market-selection','', 'Table Rescue is a conditional candidate','The product may preserve a valuable session for paid/professional or rotating-party GMs, but generic one-shot content and current emergency workflows remain strong alternatives.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-SIDE-SESSION-GATE-154','market-selection,table-rescue,conditional,one-shot'),
('F-678','portability','', 'The portable product is a neutral scenario package','A PDF plus scenario, branch, reward, and recap manifest can be run manually in Foundry, Roll20, Owlbear, or theater of the mind without an account bridge.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-SIDE-SESSION-GATE-154','portability,pdf,manifest,foundry,roll20,owlbear'),
('F-679','buyer-segmentation','', 'Table Rescue targets paid and high-variance tables','The primary buyer is a paid/professional GM, organized-play host, or rotating-party organizer; an ordinary home group that can postpone is a negative control.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-SIDE-SESSION-GATE-154','buyer,paid-gm,organized-play,rotating-party,negative-control'),
('F-680','marketability','', 'The eye-catching promise is one-click party-size recovery','A demo that switches to a two-player branch and exports a clean campaign-safe handoff is more legible than attendance management, but visual appeal cannot substitute for price choice or pilot evidence.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-SIDE-SESSION-GATE-154','marketing,eye-catching,branching,party-size,demo'),
('F-681','market-selection','', 'Table Rescue must beat exact emergency alternatives','The buyer comparison must include cancellation/refund, running short, improvising, a free one-shot, premium adventures, Drop-in Dungeons, Oronder, SessionFlow, and the GMâ€™s own emergency folder.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-SIDE-SESSION-GATE-154','competition,alternatives,drop-in,oronder,sessionflow'),
('F-682','runtime','', 'Table Rescue can avoid live campaign mutation','A disposable Foundry package can keep branches, hidden/public clue scope, rewards, and recap export isolated from the main world until the GM explicitly imports a result.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-SIDE-SESSION-GATE-154','runtime,safety,disposable-world,no-mutation,export'),
('F-683','market-selection','', 'Table Rescue remains unselected pending buyer evidence','The product needs qualified preference, non-zero price, two real pilots, and a home-table negative control before implementation.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-SIDE-SESSION-GATE-154','market-selection,price,pilot,no-product-selected'),
('F-684','rights','', 'Table Rescue should use original or licensed assets','A portable rescue scenario must not copy publisher adventures, depend on source credentials, or require a hosted account bridge.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-SIDE-SESSION-GATE-154','rights,original-assets,licensing,portable,no-hosted-service');

INSERT OR REPLACE INTO kb_decisions(decision_id,topic,decision,rationale,scope,status,owner,source_id,next_review) VALUES
('D-290','buyer-segmentation','Use paid/professional and organized-play GMs as the primary attendance cohort.','Per-session charges, no-show consequences, refunds, and event payments create a concrete economic buyer; ordinary home tables are a negative control.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-PAID-GM-ATTENDANCE-152',NULL),
('D-291','market-selection','Reject a generic attendance, booking, roster, or cancellation module.','StartPlaying and Warhorn already own the financial and scheduling workflow, while Foundry session tooling occupies broad orchestration.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-ATTENDANCE-INCUMBENT-153',NULL),
('D-292','market-selection','Retain only a content-shaped session-rescue hypothesis.','The remaining job is preserving value when the party changes, not monitoring attendance.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-ATTENDANCE-INCUMBENT-153',NULL),
('D-293','market-product-boundary','Name the candidate Table Rescue / Attendance-Resilient Side Session.','A 60â€“120 minute no-canon scenario with variable-party branches and clean export is a legible product promise over an abstract attendance tool.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-SIDE-SESSION-GATE-154',NULL),
('D-294','market-selection','Run Table Rescue at $15/$30/$49/no purchase as a qualified payer gate.','A paid/professional GM must prefer the actual scenario over cancellation, free content, premium drop-ins, and manual prep.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-SIDE-SESSION-GATE-154',NULL),
('D-295','portability','Make PDF plus neutral scenario manifest the portable baseline.','Foundry is first, but the content should run manually on other VTTs without an account bridge or hosted service.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-SIDE-SESSION-GATE-154',NULL),
('D-296','runtime','Keep Table Rescue isolated from the main campaign.','Disposable worlds, explicit export, and no hidden-state writes limit risk when a branch or reward is tested.','project','proposed','runtime','SRC-SIDE-SESSION-GATE-154',NULL),
('D-297','market-selection','Do not select Table Rescue before two pilots and a home-table control.','Attendance economics validates the segment but not scenario WTP or recurrence.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-SIDE-SESSION-GATE-154',NULL),
('D-298','rights','Use original/licensed content only and avoid hosted account bridges.','A portable rescue product should not reproduce publisher content or require source credentials.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-SIDE-SESSION-GATE-154',NULL);

INSERT OR REPLACE INTO kb_open_items(item_id,item_class,title,problem,next_action,evidence_needed,priority,status,owner,source_id) VALUES
('O-339','research','Verify the paid-session attendance consequence','A buyer may name a no-show but have no meaningful lost revenue, seat, reputation, or prep cost.','Recruit paid/professional and organized-play GMs with a dated incident and quantify the consequence.','8 qualified buyers with a concrete attendance failure and payer role.','P0','open','product-research','SRC-PAID-GM-ATTENDANCE-152'),
('O-340','research','Compare Table Rescue with the buyerâ€™s exact emergency workflow','Cancellation, refund, running short, free content, and manual prep may be cheaper and good enough.','Run a matched scenario-choice test with actual alternatives visible.','5/8 qualified preference and reason-coded alternative rejection.','P0','open','product-research','SRC-SIDE-SESSION-GATE-154'),
('O-341','research','Test Table Rescue price and payment object','The buyer may pay for a polished adventure but not the branching or Foundry packaging.','Ask $15/$30/$49/no purchase and code content, branching, presentation, and export value separately.','3/8 qualified non-zero choices with a stable payer role.','P0','open','product-research','SRC-SIDE-SESSION-GATE-154'),
('O-342','research','Test repeat or portfolio value','A single rescue scenario may be an episodic purchase and fail a broad product objective.','Offer two different party-size/genre rescue scenarios or an update/season pack and compare repeat intent.','Two pilots plus a defensible one-time or repeat purchase rationale.','P1','open','product-research','SRC-SIDE-SESSION-GATE-154'),
('O-343','implementation','Build the variable-party disposable fixture','A scenario may leak hidden state or produce duplicate rewards when branches or late joins change.','Test two/three/five-player starts, late join, absent player, reconnect, branch determinism, and explicit export.','Main campaign unchanged and deterministic reward/recap output.','P0','open','runtime','SRC-SIDE-SESSION-GATE-154'),
('O-344','implementation','Prove public/private clue boundaries','The value proposition may depend on asymmetric information that can leak through chat, journals, audio, or reconnect.','Use synthetic clues and two-player clients with reconnect and permission checks.','No unintended recipient or hidden-state disclosure.','P0','open','runtime','SRC-SIDE-SESSION-GATE-154'),
('O-345','research','Run the neutral manifest outside Foundry','Foundry automation may be the only perceived value.','Give a second-VTT or theater-of-mind tester the PDF and manifest without an account bridge.','Manual run succeeds and unsupported behavior is explicit.','P1','open','runtime','SRC-SIDE-SESSION-GATE-154'),
('O-346','research','Continue the wide search if Table Rescue is only generic content','A polished one-shot may not be a defensible VTT product.','If the candidate fails exact-alternative or price gates, open a new unrelated payer scan.','Evidence-weighted demotion and next candidate.','P1','open','product-research','SRC-SIDE-SESSION-GATE-154'),
('O-347','research','Separate attendance economics from module WTP','StartPlaying payment proves a paid GM segment, not willingness to pay for a rescue module.','Record whether buyers would pay for content, variable-party branching, Foundry packaging, or export.','Reason-coded non-zero choice.','P0','open','product-research','SRC-PAID-GM-ATTENDANCE-152'),
('O-348','implementation','Keep publisher content and source credentials out of Table Rescue','Emergency content could drift into copied adventures or account-dependent delivery.','Use original/licensed synthetic assets and no hosted account integration.','Rights matrix and negative test.','P0','open','runtime','SRC-SIDE-SESSION-GATE-154'),
('O-349','research','Keep Dungeon Master''s Forge backburnered','The fresh product search must not reopen DMF implementation scope.','Do not edit DMF; reuse only generic branching/export/validation assets after product selection.','No DMF changes and explicit backburner state.','P1','open','product-research','SRC-SIDE-SESSION-GATE-154');

INSERT OR REPLACE INTO kb_trials(trial_id,area,symptom,attempted_approach,failure_cause,correction,evidence_status,source_id) VALUES
('T-152','market-selection','Paid GM and organized-play attendance has real monetary consequences.','Treat the payment/seat signal as proof that a new attendance module will sell.','StartPlaying and Warhorn already handle booking, payment, skip, refund, and roster decisions.','Target the cost of preserving a valuable session when party size changes.','Qualified payer segment confirmed; no product selected.','SRC-PAID-GM-ATTENDANCE-152'),
('T-153','market-selection','A generic attendance dashboard or rescheduling tool was proposed.','Add roster, booking, cancellation, and session widgets to Foundry.','Direct platforms and SessionFlow occupy the broad job.','Reject infrastructure; retain only a content-shaped session-rescue hypothesis.','Incumbent correction recorded; no product selected.','SRC-ATTENDANCE-INCUMBENT-153'),
('T-154','market-selection','A no-canon rescue scenario could preserve a paid session.','Build a Foundry-only variable-party one-shot with campaign-state writes.','Generic adventure content and manual emergency prep are strong alternatives; hidden-state writes and VTT lock-in add risk.','Test Table Rescue as portable content with explicit export, price choices, two pilots, and a home-table negative control.','Conditional candidate recorded; no product selected.','SRC-SIDE-SESSION-GATE-154');

INSERT OR REPLACE INTO kb_sources(source_id,title,source_kind,scope,authority,status,location,captured_at,version_fingerprint,notes) VALUES
('SRC-SESSION-RELIABILITY-155','Session reliability recurring-pain scan','project','project','Current community reports plus Foundry troubleshooting guidance for scene, connection, asset, browser/GPU, and module failures','active','..\\PRODUCT_RESEARCH.md','2026-09-26','155 player-session reliability scan','Recurring session disruption confirmed; universal network repair is outside a module boundary'),
('SRC-SESSION-RELIABILITY-INCUMBENT-156','Session reliability incumbent correction','project','project','Connection Monitor, Performance Optimizer, Preloader, core scene/preload/backups, and troubleshooting guidance','active','..\\PRODUCT_RESEARCH.md','2026-09-26','156 reliability/performance/recovery incumbent correction','Reject generic performance or connection product; retain readiness and safe rejoin hypothesis'),
('SRC-SESSION-CONTINUITY-GATE-157','Session Continuity product gate','project','project','Foundry reliability controls, player failure reports, recovery boundary, and cross-VTT receipt model','active','..\\PRODUCT_RESEARCH.md','2026-09-26','157 client-health/rejoin-receipt product gate','Conditional reliability candidate; no product selected');

INSERT OR REPLACE INTO kb_facts(fact_id,domain,subject_no,title,statement,scope,evidence_class,status,source_id,tags) VALUES
('F-685','buyer-pain','', 'Players can be connected but unable to play','Community reports describe players losing token movement, scene visibility, actor visibility, or interaction until refresh/reconnect, creating repeated session disruption.','project','static','provisional','SRC-SESSION-RELIABILITY-155','buyer-pain,player,disconnect,scene,interaction'),
('F-686','buyer-pain','', 'Foundry reliability failures have multiple root causes','Foundry identifies module conflicts, oversized images, hardware acceleration, missing assets, disk space, and network conditions as different scene-loading causes.','project','static','provisional','SRC-SESSION-RELIABILITY-155','buyer-pain,scene-loading,network,gpu,assets,module-conflict'),
('F-687','buyer-segmentation','', 'Paid and high-investment tables have a stronger reliability consequence','A paid GM, organized host, or long-running campaign owner loses session time, money, reputation, or player trust when a table must restart.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-SESSION-RELIABILITY-155','buyer,paid-gm,campaign,session-cost,reputation'),
('F-688','market-product-boundary','', 'A Foundry module cannot promise universal network repair','Router, ISP, browser, GPU, hosting, and arbitrary module-conflict causes are not all observable or fixable from a local add-on.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-SESSION-RELIABILITY-155','boundary,network,hosting,browser,gpu,no-guarantee'),
('F-689','market-selection','', 'Session Continuity should measure safe continuation','The defensible job is distinguishing connected, interactive, scene-ready, and current clients, then exposing an explicit recovery path.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-SESSION-RELIABILITY-155','market-selection,readiness,continuity,client-health'),
('F-690','competition','', 'Connection Monitor already covers basic disconnect state','Connection Monitor detects disconnections/reconnections and visually disables or de-emphasizes controls while disconnected, but does not prove scene readiness or recover uncertain actions.','project','static','provisional','SRC-SESSION-RELIABILITY-INCUMBENT-156','competition,connection-monitor,disconnect,ui'),
('F-691','competition','', 'Performance Optimizer covers client rendering health','Performance Optimizer provides per-player profiles, low-FPS detection, GM controls, and a benchmark/live FPS view, so a generic performance panel is occupied.','project','static','provisional','SRC-SESSION-RELIABILITY-INCUMBENT-156','competition,performance-optimizer,fps,client-health'),
('F-692','competition','', 'Core Foundry covers several preload and recovery controls','Core provides scene preload, safe configuration, package backups, and snapshots, so Session Continuity must not repackage those controls without decision-changing evidence.','project','static','provisional','SRC-SESSION-RELIABILITY-INCUMBENT-156','competition,core,preload,safe-mode,backup,snapshot'),
('F-693','market-selection','', 'Generic connection and hosting products are rejected','Hosting, browser/GPU fixes, network repair, and general connection banners are exact alternatives or outside the module boundary.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-SESSION-RELIABILITY-INCUMBENT-156','market-selection,hosting,network,performance,rejected'),
('F-694','market-product-boundary','', 'The residual wedge is a reliability receipt and recovery workflow','The gap is an evidence-linked â€œsafe to continue / waiting / unknownâ€ answer with scene identity, readiness signals, last confirmed event, and explicit pending action.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-SESSION-RELIABILITY-INCUMBENT-156','product-boundary,receipt,readiness,unknown,pending-action'),
('F-695','market-selection','', 'Session Continuity is a conditional recurring-pain candidate','A client-health and safe-rejoin layer could serve paid or high-investment tables, but existing controls and hosting remain strong alternatives.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-SESSION-CONTINUITY-GATE-157','market-selection,session-continuity,conditional,rejoin'),
('F-696','runtime','', 'Safe rejoin must not replay uncertain actions','A disconnected or stale client may have submitted, partially submitted, or never submitted an action; recovery must preserve uncertainty rather than guess or mutate the world.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-SESSION-CONTINUITY-GATE-157','runtime,safety,uncertain-action,no-replay'),
('F-697','portability','', 'The portable artifact is a neutral health/recovery receipt','A receipt can carry client/session/scene identity, readiness, last confirmed server event, pending/unknown action, and unsupported state without sharing player content or requiring a hosted bridge.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-SESSION-CONTINUITY-GATE-157','portability,receipt,manifest,health,recovery'),
('F-698','marketability','', 'The eye-catching demo is proof of who can safely continue','A GM sees exactly which player is interactive and ready while a reconnecting player receives a clear scene and unsent-action status; the demo is legible without claiming network repair.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-SESSION-CONTINUITY-GATE-157','marketing,eye-catching,gm,player,rejoin'),
('F-699','market-selection','', 'Session Continuity must beat exact controls','The buyer comparison includes Connection Monitor, Performance Optimizer, core preload/safe mode, backups, hosting support, browser/GPU fixes, and refreshing.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-SESSION-CONTINUITY-GATE-157','competition,alternatives,price,control'),
('F-700','market-selection','', 'Session Continuity remains unselected pending pilots','Qualified preference, non-zero price, multi-session pilots, and a home-table negative control are required before implementation.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-SESSION-CONTINUITY-GATE-157','market-selection,price,pilot,no-product-selected'),

('F-701','rights','', 'Session Continuity can avoid content and credential collection','A health/recovery receipt can be generated from local/session metadata without uploading player content, collecting credentials, or operating a hosted service.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-SESSION-CONTINUITY-GATE-157','rights,privacy,metadata,no-content,credentials');

INSERT OR REPLACE INTO kb_decisions(decision_id,topic,decision,rationale,scope,status,owner,source_id,next_review) VALUES
('D-299','market-selection','Open Session Continuity as a recurring reliability hypothesis.','Player-visible disconnect, stale scene, and interaction failures recur and carry high session cost, but root causes are diverse.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-SESSION-RELIABILITY-155',NULL),
('D-300','market-product-boundary','Do not promise universal connection or network repair.','Router, ISP, browser, GPU, hosting, and arbitrary module conflicts exceed a local add-on boundary.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-SESSION-RELIABILITY-155',NULL),
('D-301','buyer-segmentation','Recruit paid/professional and high-investment campaign buyers first.','Their lost time, revenue, reputation, and player trust create stronger WTP than a table that can casually restart.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-SESSION-RELIABILITY-155',NULL),
('D-302','market-selection','Reject generic performance, connection, and hosting products.','Connection Monitor, Performance Optimizer, core preload/safe mode, backups, hosting, and browser/GPU fixes occupy adjacent jobs.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-SESSION-RELIABILITY-INCUMBENT-156',NULL),
('D-303','market-product-boundary','Define Session Continuity as a readiness receipt and safe-rejoin workflow.','The residual decision is whether the table can safely continue and what is confirmed, pending, or unknown.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-SESSION-RELIABILITY-INCUMBENT-156',NULL),
('D-304','runtime','Never replay an uncertain action or mutate the world during recovery.','A stale client cannot prove whether an action reached the server; preserving uncertainty is safer than guessing.','project','proposed','runtime','SRC-SESSION-CONTINUITY-GATE-157',NULL),
('D-305','market-selection','Run Session Continuity at $10/$20/$40/no purchase as a qualified gate.','The buyer must pay for diagnosis, safe rejoin, action-loss prevention, or GM confidence rather than a free banner.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-SESSION-CONTINUITY-GATE-157',NULL),
('D-306','portability','Use a neutral health/recovery receipt as the cross-VTT baseline.','Other VTTs can consume evidence or a checklist without claiming identical networking or runtime behavior.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-SESSION-CONTINUITY-GATE-157',NULL),
('D-307','market-selection','Do not select Session Continuity before two pilots and a home-table control.','Current evidence confirms pain and alternatives but not module-specific WTP.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-SESSION-CONTINUITY-GATE-157',NULL);

INSERT OR REPLACE INTO kb_open_items(item_id,item_class,title,problem,next_action,evidence_needed,priority,status,owner,source_id) VALUES
('O-350','research','Recruit buyers with a dated reliability failure','General frustration with Foundry is not enough; the buyer must have lost session time, money, or trust.','Recruit paid/professional GMs and high-investment campaign owners with a reproducible incident.','8 qualified buyers with payer role and quantified consequence.','P0','open','product-research','SRC-SESSION-RELIABILITY-155'),
('O-351','research','Separate root causes from module-solvable symptoms','Network, browser/GPU, disk, asset, module, and permission problems can look similar.','Classify each failure before showing the candidate.','Root-cause matrix and false-green/unknown handling.','P0','open','product-research','SRC-SESSION-RELIABILITY-155'),
('O-352','research','Compare Session Continuity with Connection Monitor','A free module already detects disconnect/reconnect state.','Run matched failure fixtures and code decision-changing evidence.','5/8 qualified buyers prefer beyond the free control.','P0','open','product-research','SRC-SESSION-RELIABILITY-INCUMBENT-156'),
('O-353','research','Compare Session Continuity with Performance Optimizer','Low FPS can present as lag or non-responsiveness.','Test low-FPS, network, and stale-scene cases separately.','Candidate identifies a different actionable state.','P0','open','product-research','SRC-SESSION-RELIABILITY-INCUMBENT-156'),
('O-354','research','Compare Session Continuity with core preload/safe mode/backups','Foundry already has preload, safe configuration, and recovery controls.','Run the same scenario with core controls first.','Receipt changes a continue/restart/recover decision.','P1','open','product-research','SRC-SESSION-RELIABILITY-INCUMBENT-156'),
('O-355','implementation','Build a two-client readiness fixture','A client may be connected but stale, loading, interactive, or on the wrong scene.','Track connection, heartbeat, interaction, scene identity, required assets, and server-confirmed event.','Deterministic safe/waiting/unknown states.','P0','open','runtime','SRC-SESSION-CONTINUITY-GATE-157'),
('O-356','implementation','Prove safe rejoin without action replay','Recovery could duplicate attacks, moves, rolls, or state changes.','Use staged synthetic actions with dropped connection and delayed reconnect.','No duplicate mutation; pending/unknown remains explicit.','P0','open','runtime','SRC-SESSION-CONTINUITY-GATE-157'),
('O-357','implementation','Test scene and asset readiness','Black/gray scenes and missing assets may be mistaken for disconnection.','Use missing file, oversized image, module conflict, GPU warning, and disk/network fixtures.','Distinct causes or explicit unknown; no false green.','P0','open','runtime','SRC-SESSION-CONTINUITY-GATE-157'),
('O-358','research','Test Session Continuity price and payment object','Buyers may want hosting or free diagnostics instead of a paid module.','Ask $10/$20/$40/no purchase and code diagnosis, rejoin, action-loss, and confidence value.','3/8 qualified non-zero choices.','P0','open','product-research','SRC-SESSION-CONTINUITY-GATE-157'),
('O-359','research','Run two multi-session pilots','A single successful reconnect may not support recurring value.','Test normal session, failure session, and a later session with the same table.','Two pilots with repeated use or a defensible one-time price.','P1','open','product-research','SRC-SESSION-CONTINUITY-GATE-157'),
('O-360','research','Continue the wide search if reliability is only a support feature','A helpful diagnostic may not be a standalone product.','If exact alternatives solve the case or buyers reject price, open the next unrelated payer scan.','Evidence-weighted demotion and new candidate.','P1','open','product-research','SRC-SESSION-CONTINUITY-GATE-157');

INSERT OR REPLACE INTO kb_trials(trial_id,area,symptom,attempted_approach,failure_cause,correction,evidence_status,source_id) VALUES
('T-155','market-selection','Players repeatedly lose scene, input, or synchronization state.','Treat the reliability problem as a universal connection-fix opportunity.','Foundry documents multiple root causes outside an add-on boundary.','Open a client-health and safe-rejoin hypothesis without network-repair claims.','Recurring pain confirmed; no product selected.','SRC-SESSION-RELIABILITY-155'),
('T-156','market-selection','A generic connection/performance module was proposed.','Add a disconnect banner, FPS panel, preload controls, and hosting advice.','Connection Monitor, Performance Optimizer, core controls, and hosting support occupy those jobs.','Retain only evidence-linked readiness and recovery as the residual wedge.','Incumbent correction recorded; no product selected.','SRC-SESSION-RELIABILITY-INCUMBENT-156'),
('T-157','market-selection','A readiness receipt could help a GM decide whether to continue.','Build a Foundry-only recovery tool that replays or repairs uncertain actions.','Stale clients cannot prove whether an action reached the server, and VTT runtime parity is not portable.','Test Session Continuity with no replay, explicit unknown states, neutral receipts, qualified pricing, and two pilots.','Conditional candidate recorded; no product selected.','SRC-SESSION-CONTINUITY-GATE-157');

INSERT OR REPLACE INTO kb_sources(source_id,title,source_kind,scope,authority,status,location,captured_at,version_fingerprint,notes) VALUES
('SRC-REST-DOWNTIME-158','Rest and downtime recurring-pain scan','project','project','Current Foundry community reports about rest bottlenecks and ordinary D&D resource bookkeeping','active','..\\PRODUCT_RESEARCH.md','2026-09-26','158 rest/downtime ordinary-table scan','Recurring player and GM time cost confirmed; broad automation remains unproven'),
('SRC-REST-INCUMBENT-159','Rest-management incumbent correction','project','project','Rest Recovery 5e, Ionrift Respite, Stress Points & Rest, Character Builder, and community response','active','..\\PRODUCT_RESEARCH.md','2026-09-26','159 rest/recovery/current-module correction','Reject broad rest engine; retain neutral activity and approval contracts'),
('SRC-REST-DEMOTION-160','Rest content and portability demotion','project','project','Ionrift event-pack and multi-system surface, Stress Points & Rest, system-native rest controls','active','..\\PRODUCT_RESEARCH.md','2026-09-26','160 rest-content/portability demotion','Rest remains a negative control; no product selected');

INSERT OR REPLACE INTO kb_facts(fact_id,domain,subject_no,title,statement,scope,evidence_class,status,source_id,tags) VALUES
('F-702','buyer-pain','', 'Rest logistics create a recurring session bottleneck','Community evidence describes long rests as a sequence of GM-mediated identify, attune, copy-spell, watch, food, equipment, and recovery requests that can consume about an hour.','project','static','provisional','SRC-REST-DOWNTIME-158','buyer-pain,rest,downtime,bookkeeping,gm-time'),
('F-703','buyer-segmentation','', 'Ordinary D&D players are directly affected by rest workflow','Every D&D5e table encounters short or long rests, and players either lose session time or skip meaningful downtime choices when the process is too manual.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-REST-DOWNTIME-158','buyer,players,dnd5e,rest,session-time'),
('F-704','market-product-boundary','', 'Rest automation must hand off to the authoritative system engine','Different tables choose different rest timing, food, exhaustion, downtime, recovery, and homebrew rules, so a product cannot assume one universal rest semantics.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-REST-DOWNTIME-158','boundary,rest,homebrew,system-engine,semantics'),
('F-705','market-selection','', 'A portable rest artifact can describe workflow but not identical rules','Activities, approvals, costs, checks, and results can be represented neutrally, while resource recovery and system hooks require VTT/system adapters.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-REST-DOWNTIME-158','portability,manifest,activities,approval,adapter'),
('F-706','buyer-pain','', 'Rest interest is not automatically payment intent','The presence of a recurring rest bottleneck establishes need, but a table may prefer skipping detail, using a free module, or changing house rules.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-REST-DOWNTIME-158','buyer-pain,wtp,free-alternative,house-rules'),
('F-707','competition','', 'Rest Recovery 5e covers the broad D&D5e recovery job','Rest Recovery 5e is current for Foundry 14 and covers class features, HP, partial recovery, exhaustion, food, water, starvation, and optional long-rest behavior.','project','static','provisional','SRC-REST-INCUMBENT-159','competition,rest-recovery,dnd5e,foundry14,exhaustion'),
('F-708','competition','', 'Ionrift Respite covers self-service rest and downtime','Ionrift Respite is current for Foundry 14 and provides player activities, GM-reviewed events, comfort, meals, recovery, short-rest flow, identify, attune, copy spell, custom event packs, and multiple system adapters.','project','static','provisional','SRC-REST-INCUMBENT-159','competition,ionrift,respite,self-service,event-pack,multi-system'),
('F-709','competition','', 'Stress Points & Rest occupies the survival-pressure variant','Stress Points & Rest adds stress, food, drink, comfort, medical supplies, environment checks, and purchases to the D&D5e rest loop.','project','static','provisional','SRC-REST-INCUMBENT-159','competition,stress,rest,survival,food,comfort'),
('F-710','competition','', 'Character Builder already coordinates rest gating and compatibility','D&D5e Character Builder can manage GM-controlled rest availability and coordinates with Rest Recovery while handing authoritative rest execution back to D&D5e.','project','static','provisional','SRC-REST-INCUMBENT-159','competition,character-builder,rest-gating,compatibility'),
('F-711','market-selection','', 'Free module enthusiasm does not prove rest-product WTP','Ionrift community responses show strong appreciation for its free/non-commercial solution, but praise and sharing intent do not establish a non-zero price for a competing product.','project','static','provisional','SRC-REST-INCUMBENT-159','market-selection,wtp,free,enthusiasm,ionrift'),
('F-712','market-selection','', 'A generic rest engine is rejected','Rest Recovery 5e, Ionrift Respite, Stress Points & Rest, Character Builder, native system rests, and manual workflows occupy the broad rest surface.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-REST-INCUMBENT-159','market-selection,rest,rejected,incumbent'),
('F-713','competition','', 'A rest event pack is also occupied','Ionrift already includes terrain-specific branching events and a custom event-pack schema, reducing differentiation for another generic camp-event product.','project','static','provisional','SRC-REST-DEMOTION-160','competition,event-pack,ionrift,content'),
('F-714','portability','', 'Rest portability has a large adapter burden','Rest timing, resource recovery, exhaustion, item hooks, approvals, and system-specific activities differ across VTTs and game systems.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-REST-DEMOTION-160','portability,adapter,system,rules,rest'),
('F-715','market-selection','', 'Rest content remains a ruleset-specific possibility only','A qualified buyer might pay for a specific unresolved ruleset or event workflow, but the broad ordinary-table product case is closed until an exact failure survives the current stack.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-REST-DEMOTION-160','market-selection,ruleset,content,narrow'),
('F-716','market-selection','', 'Rest and downtime are demoted as a product','Need is real but current free/current alternatives, compatibility burden, and absent product-specific WTP fail the selection gate.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-REST-DEMOTION-160','market-selection,demoted,no-product-selected');

INSERT OR REPLACE INTO kb_decisions(decision_id,topic,decision,rationale,scope,status,owner,source_id,next_review) VALUES
('D-308','market-selection','Open rest/downtime as a high-frequency ordinary-table scan.','Rest logistics can consume session time and affect every D&D5e table.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-REST-DOWNTIME-158',NULL),
('D-309','market-product-boundary','Require player self-service and GM approval handoff for any rest hypothesis.','Rest rules and homebrew vary, and system-native engines remain authoritative.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-REST-DOWNTIME-158',NULL),
('D-310','portability','Retain neutral activity, approval, cost, check, and result contracts.','Those concepts can travel, while rest semantics require adapters.','project','proposed','runtime','SRC-REST-DOWNTIME-158',NULL),
('D-311','market-selection','Reject a broad rest/recovery automation product.','Rest Recovery 5e, Ionrift Respite, Stress Points & Rest, Character Builder, and native controls cover the broad job.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-REST-INCUMBENT-159',NULL),
('D-312','market-selection','Do not infer rest-product WTP from free-module enthusiasm.','Ionrift responses validate need and appreciation, not a non-zero price for a competitor.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-REST-INCUMBENT-159',NULL),
('D-313','market-selection','Reject a generic premium rest-event pack.','Ionrift already provides branching events and custom event-pack support.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-REST-DEMOTION-160',NULL),
('D-314','market-selection','Keep rest/downtime as a negative control.','No unresolved broad job survives current alternatives and portability is weak.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-REST-DEMOTION-160',NULL),
('D-315','market-selection','Reopen rest only for a named ruleset-specific failure.','A narrow buyer may still pay for an unresolved workflow, but it must beat exact current controls and complete a pilot.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-REST-DEMOTION-160',NULL),
('D-316','market-selection','Continue the wide search for a stronger product.','The active goal requires product-specific WTP, not merely recurring pain.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-REST-DEMOTION-160',NULL);

INSERT OR REPLACE INTO kb_open_items(item_id,item_class,title,problem,next_action,evidence_needed,priority,status,owner,source_id) VALUES
('O-361','research','Quantify rest bottleneck cost','Rest frustration may not create a buyer-level consequence.','Recruit tables with a dated rest delay and measure minutes, skipped choices, or GM interruption.','8 tables with a reproducible cost and payer role.','P1','open','product-research','SRC-REST-DOWNTIME-158'),
('O-362','research','Compare native rest workflow with current modules','A new tool may solve nothing beyond native or installed controls.','Run matched rest fixtures through native D&D5e, Rest Recovery, Ionrift, Stress Points, and Character Builder.','Named unresolved failure.','P0','open','product-research','SRC-REST-INCUMBENT-159'),
('O-363','research','Separate need from payment intent','Free module praise and sharing may be mistaken for WTP.','Ask $10/$20/$40/no purchase only after exact alternatives.','3/8 non-zero price choices for a specific job.','P0','open','product-research','SRC-REST-INCUMBENT-159'),
('O-364','implementation','Preserve authoritative rest handoff','A competing rest engine could double-apply recovery or corrupt system resources.','Use native rest completion events and idempotent transaction boundaries.','No duplicate recovery in two systems.','P0','open','runtime','SRC-REST-DOWNTIME-158'),
('O-365','implementation','Test activity and approval portability','Activity schemas may not map to system actions or permissions.','Create a neutral activity fixture with unsupported states.','Second-VTT manual consumer and explicit unsupported output.','P1','open','runtime','SRC-REST-DOWNTIME-158'),
('O-366','research','Test ruleset-specific reopening condition','A narrow failure may survive the generic demotion.','Ask D&D5e/PF2e/OSR tables for a named unresolved rest action and exact workaround.','Repeatable failure and payer identity.','P2','open','product-research','SRC-REST-DEMOTION-160'),
('O-367','research','Do not copy current event packs','Another event library would be weak differentiation and a rights risk.','Use original/licensed content only if a narrow gate reopens.','Rights matrix and non-copying proof.','P1','open','runtime','SRC-REST-DEMOTION-160'),
('O-368','research','Continue the wide search after rest demotion','Rest is real but occupied and weak on product-specific WTP.','Open the next unrelated ordinary-table payer scan.','New candidate or negative control.','P0','open','product-research','SRC-REST-DEMOTION-160'),
('O-369','implementation','Keep activity/approval/event contracts reusable only','Reusable schemas must not become an unvalidated product commitment.','Store neutral contracts without starting a rest implementation.','No rest package scope added.','P2','open','runtime','SRC-REST-DEMOTION-160'),
('O-370','research','Keep Dungeon Master''s Forge backburnered','The negative rest pass must not reopen DMF scope.','Do not edit DMF; reuse only generic contract assets later if selected.','No DMF changes and explicit backburner status.','P1','open','product-research','SRC-REST-DEMOTION-160');

INSERT OR REPLACE INTO kb_trials(trial_id,area,symptom,attempted_approach,failure_cause,correction,evidence_status,source_id) VALUES
('T-158','market-selection','Rest and downtime bookkeeping can consume substantial session time.','Treat recurring rest pain as proof that a new rest engine will sell.','Rules vary and current modules may already solve the workflow.','Open an exact-alternative and price gate.','Recurring pain confirmed; no product selected.','SRC-REST-DOWNTIME-158'),
('T-159','market-selection','A broad self-service rest module was proposed.','Build player activities, recovery, food, events, and approvals as a new module.','Rest Recovery, Ionrift, Stress Points, Character Builder, and native controls occupy the job; free-module enthusiasm is not WTP.','Reject the broad engine and retain neutral contracts.','Incumbent correction recorded; no product selected.','SRC-REST-INCUMBENT-159'),
('T-160','market-selection','A premium rest-event/content pack was considered.','Compete with current event libraries using portable camp scenes.','Ionrift supports branching events, custom packs, and multiple systems; portability and rights are weak.','Demote rest as a negative control and continue the wide search.','Product demotion recorded; no product selected.','SRC-REST-DEMOTION-160');

INSERT OR REPLACE INTO kb_sources(source_id,title,source_kind,scope,authority,status,location,captured_at,version_fingerprint,notes) VALUES
('SRC-MEDIA-PLAYABILITY-161','Map and media playability scan','project','project','Foundry media/troubleshooting guidance plus recent community reports of black screens, stalled loads, and browser/media failures','active','..\\PRODUCT_RESEARCH.md','2026-09-26','161 map/media recurring-pain scan','Asset-heavy sessions have a concrete player cost; optimization must preserve fidelity and rollback'),
('SRC-MEDIA-INCUMBENT-162','Media optimizer incumbent correction','project','project','Geano Scene Optimizer, DF Architect, official media and asset guidance, external tools, preload, and hosting','active','..\\PRODUCT_RESEARCH.md','2026-09-26','162 media-converter/direct-incumbent correction','Reject generic conversion; retain verified playability and rollback hypothesis'),
('SRC-PLAYABILITY-BUDGET-GATE-163','Playability Budget product gate','project','project','User-owned media fixture, client-risk receipt, optimized variants, portability, and rights boundary','active','..\\PRODUCT_RESEARCH.md','2026-09-26','163 asset-risk/optimization/rollback product gate','Conditional candidate; no product selected');

INSERT OR REPLACE INTO kb_facts(fact_id,domain,subject_no,title,statement,scope,evidence_class,status,source_id,tags) VALUES
('F-717','buyer-pain','', 'Large or unoptimized media can strand players','Community reports describe black screens, stalled loads, very long waits, and screen sharing when maps, videos, or assets are too large or incompatible.','project','static','provisional','SRC-MEDIA-PLAYABILITY-161','buyer-pain,media,map,black-screen,stalled-load'),
('F-718','competition','', 'Foundry recommends asset formats and budgets','Foundry recommends WebP/OGG-style efficient formats, notes that scene media is distributed to connected users, and suggests keeping video maps near 50 MB when possible.','project','static','provisional','SRC-MEDIA-PLAYABILITY-161','competition,media,webp,ogg,video,budget'),
('F-719','buyer-segmentation','', 'Asset-heavy GMs have a recurring playability cost','GMs who buy or create map-heavy content, paid hosts, and campaign owners can lose session time or exclude a player when media fails.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-MEDIA-PLAYABILITY-161','buyer,gm,paid-host,map-heavy,player-exclusion'),
('F-720','market-product-boundary','', 'Compression alone is not playability proof','A smaller file can still fail because of pixel dimensions, codec, browser/GPU, missing path, disk, or network conditions.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-MEDIA-PLAYABILITY-161','boundary,compression,codec,gpu,network,playability'),
('F-721','market-selection','', 'Playability Budget is a new conditional candidate','A local read-only scanner that estimates per-client risk and creates confirmed non-destructive variants may solve a different job from conversion.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-MEDIA-PLAYABILITY-161','market-selection,playability-budget,receipt,optimization'),
('F-722','competition','', 'Geano Scene Optimizer already converts common media','Geano Scene Optimizer detects scene/audio formats, converts images to WebP and audio to OGG/Opus, preserves originals, and shows progress.','project','static','provisional','SRC-MEDIA-INCUMBENT-162','competition,geano,webp,ogg,conversion,rollback'),
('F-723','competition','', 'DF Architect occupies flattening and scene-prep control','DF Architect provides tile flattening and map-prep features, but its package page reports an older verified Foundry release.','project','static','provisional','SRC-MEDIA-INCUMBENT-162','competition,df-architect,flattening,scene-prep,version'),
('F-724','competition','', 'Official guidance and free external tools are strong controls','Foundry''s media/asset guides, Audacity, image converters, ffmpeg, core preload, hosting, and S3 can solve parts of the optimization job without a new module.','project','static','provisional','SRC-MEDIA-INCUMBENT-162','competition,official-guide,audacity,ffmpeg,preload,s3'),
('F-725','market-product-boundary','', 'The residual gap is verified playability and rollback','A differentiated product must report risk for declared clients, compare fidelity/audio behavior, preserve originals, and link every optimized copy to rollback.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-MEDIA-INCUMBENT-162','product-boundary,playability,rollback,fidelity,client-risk'),
('F-726','market-selection','', 'Generic media conversion is rejected','A converter that only reduces bytes will be displaced by current modules and free tools.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-MEDIA-INCUMBENT-162','market-selection,converter,rejected,free-tools'),
('F-727','market-selection','', 'Playability Budget targets a qualified GM payer','The buyer is an asset-heavy GM, paid host, or campaign owner with a named loading failure; small-map home tables are a negative control.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-PLAYABILITY-BUDGET-GATE-163','buyer,paid-gm,asset-heavy,negative-control'),
('F-728','runtime','', 'Playability Budget can be local and non-destructive','The product can scan user-owned files, write optimized copies only after confirmation, preserve originals, and avoid live-world mutation.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-PLAYABILITY-BUDGET-GATE-163','runtime,local,non-destructive,rollback,no-mutation'),
('F-729','portability','', 'The portable artifact is an asset-risk manifest','A manifest can carry hashes, dimensions, codecs, budgets, checks, optimized variants, unsupported states, and rollback paths for manual use in another VTT.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-PLAYABILITY-BUDGET-GATE-163','portability,manifest,hash,codec,unsupported'),
('F-730','marketability','', 'The eye-catching demo is weakest-client verification','A GM can see a large scene move from probable failure to verified under a low-bandwidth/low-GPU fixture while retaining the original.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-PLAYABILITY-BUDGET-GATE-163','marketing,eye-catching,low-gpu,low-bandwidth,verification'),
('F-731','market-selection','', 'Playability Budget remains unselected pending payment and pilots','Qualified preference, a non-zero price, two pilots, and a home-table negative control are required before implementation.','project','created_document','provisional','SRC-PLAYABILITY-BUDGET-GATE-163','market-selection,price,pilot,no-product-selected');

INSERT OR REPLACE INTO kb_decisions(decision_id,topic,decision,rationale,scope,status,owner,source_id,next_review) VALUES
('D-317','market-selection','Open Playability Budget / Media Safe Pack as a conditional candidate.','Large media can directly strand players and create a concrete GM cost.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-MEDIA-PLAYABILITY-161',NULL),
('D-318','market-product-boundary','Do not promise universal browser, GPU, network, or hosting repair.','Those causes exceed a local asset tool boundary.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-MEDIA-PLAYABILITY-161',NULL),
('D-319','market-selection','Reject a generic media converter.','Geano Scene Optimizer, DF Architect, official guidance, external tools, preload, and hosting occupy byte-reduction and preparation jobs.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-MEDIA-INCUMBENT-162',NULL),
('D-320','market-product-boundary','Define the residual product as client-risk assurance plus rollback.','The buyer needs to know whether the exact world is playable and recover safely, not merely reduce file size.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-MEDIA-INCUMBENT-162',NULL),
('D-321','buyer-segmentation','Recruit asset-heavy and paid/professional GMs first.','They have named failure, player exclusion, refund, and preparation cost; small-map home tables are a negative control.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-PLAYABILITY-BUDGET-GATE-163',NULL),
('D-322','market-selection','Run Playability Budget at $10/$25/$50/no purchase.','A price choice must be attached to diagnosis, exclusion prevention, conversion, or rollback confidence.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-PLAYABILITY-BUDGET-GATE-163',NULL),
('D-323','runtime','Keep the tool local, read-only by default, and non-destructive.','User-owned assets and originals must remain safe; live-world mutation is not needed for the proof.','project','proposed','runtime','SRC-PLAYABILITY-BUDGET-GATE-163',NULL),
('D-324','portability','Use an asset-risk manifest as the cross-VTT baseline.','Other VTTs can consume reports or optimized files manually without identical runtime claims.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-PLAYABILITY-BUDGET-GATE-163',NULL),
('D-325','market-selection','Do not select Playability Budget before two pilots and a home-table control.','Current evidence confirms pain and a technical wedge but not product-specific WTP.','project','proposed','product-research','SRC-PLAYABILITY-BUDGET-GATE-163',NULL);

INSERT OR REPLACE INTO kb_open_items(item_id,item_class,title,problem,next_action,evidence_needed,priority,status,owner,source_id) VALUES
('O-371','research','Recruit buyers with a dated media failure','General appreciation for fast loading is not payment evidence.','Recruit asset-heavy and paid/professional GMs with quantified consequence.','8 qualified buyers and payer role.','P0','open','product-research','SRC-MEDIA-PLAYABILITY-161'),
('O-372','research','Separate asset failure from network/browser failure','Black screens and stalls have multiple causes that an optimizer may not solve.','Classify failures with a root-cause fixture before pricing.','Cause matrix and explicit unknown output.','P0','open','product-research','SRC-MEDIA-PLAYABILITY-161'),
('O-373','research','Compare Geano Scene Optimizer directly','A current converter may already solve the buyer job.','Run matched assets through Geano and the candidate.','Decision-changing evidence beyond conversion.','P0','open','product-research','SRC-MEDIA-INCUMBENT-162'),
('O-374','research','Compare DF Architect and external tools','Flattening and command-line tools may be sufficient.','Run the same scene through flattening, WebP/OGG, ffmpeg, and manual workflow.','5/8 preference over exact alternatives.','P0','open','product-research','SRC-MEDIA-INCUMBENT-162'),
('O-375','implementation','Build a client-risk fixture','Per-client risk needs more than file size.','Test dimensions, codecs, disk, bandwidth, GPU, browser, and preload.','Deterministic risk report and unsupported states.','P0','open','runtime','SRC-PLAYABILITY-BUDGET-GATE-163'),
('O-376','implementation','Prove visual and audio fidelity','Optimization can create artifacts, broken loops, or unusable paths.','Compare original/optimized assets and exercise scene/audio playback.','Human-reviewable diff and rollback.','P0','open','runtime','SRC-PLAYABILITY-BUDGET-GATE-163'),
('O-377','implementation','Preserve rollback and world safety','Writing optimized paths into a live world could break content.','Write side-by-side copies and explicit staged changes only.','Originals unchanged and rollback link works.','P0','open','runtime','SRC-PLAYABILITY-BUDGET-GATE-163'),
('O-378','research','Test Playability Budget price object','Buyers may only want conversion or hosting.','Ask $10/$25/$50/no purchase and code diagnosis, conversion, exclusion prevention, and rollback value.','3/8 qualified non-zero choices.','P0','open','product-research','SRC-PLAYABILITY-BUDGET-GATE-163'),
('O-379','research','Run two multi-world or multi-session pilots','A one-time map conversion may not support a product.','Test new map packs, campaign updates, and a later player/client profile.','Two pilots with repeat or defensible one-time price.','P1','open','product-research','SRC-PLAYABILITY-BUDGET-GATE-163'),
('O-380','research','Keep Dungeon Master''s Forge backburnered','The fresh asset scan must not reopen DMF scope.','Do not edit DMF; reuse only generic asset receipt/rollback contracts later.','No DMF changes and explicit backburner status.','P1','open','product-research','SRC-PLAYABILITY-BUDGET-GATE-163');

INSERT OR REPLACE INTO kb_trials(trial_id,area,symptom,attempted_approach,failure_cause,correction,evidence_status,source_id) VALUES
('T-161','market-selection','Large or unoptimized media can strand players and waste a session.','Treat compression alone as a marketable product.','Different root causes and existing guidance/tools make byte reduction insufficient.','Open a client-risk, playability, and rollback hypothesis.','Recurring pain confirmed; no product selected.','SRC-MEDIA-PLAYABILITY-161'),
('T-162','market-selection','A generic scene/audio optimizer was proposed.','Convert all assets to smaller formats.','Geano Scene Optimizer, DF Architect, official guidance, external tools, preload, and hosting occupy the broad job.','Retain verified playability and rollback as the residual wedge.','Incumbent correction recorded; no product selected.','SRC-MEDIA-INCUMBENT-162'),
('T-163','market-selection','A playability receipt could prevent weakest-client failure.','Build a destructive optimizer that rewrites live worlds.','Blind conversion can reduce fidelity or break paths; portability requires a neutral artifact.','Test Playability Budget as local, non-destructive assurance with staged variants, rollback, price choices, and two pilots.','Conditional candidate recorded; no product selected.','SRC-PLAYABILITY-BUDGET-GATE-163');

